(:file :tree "tc1" :path "asl/grammar/tools.asn" :text "(:tools :v 2 :substrate \"ASL\"\n  :doc \"Authoritative machine-readable registry of operational Pure-ASN S-expressions for autonomous agents. Agents execute operations exclusively via these forms.\"\n  :t0 \"AgentScript (asl) runs batch file operations on the git repository containing the working directory. Reach for it for targeted symbol reads instead of dumping files, definitions plus uses in one step, and atomic edits validated before disk commit. Edits and writes stage in a session buffer on disk that persists across calls; (:diff), (:check) and (:test) see staged content, (:flush) writes it, (:discard) drops it. asl exits 0 on success, 1 on rejected forms, and 2 on syntax or balance errors. Forms can also come from a file, asl -f FILE, or from stdin, asl -, with the same batch and exit codes; a heredoc with a quoted delimiter (asl - <<'ASN') passes a form holding a single quote, which asl '...' cannot. Discover operations via (:tools) for the full registry, (:help :op <name>) for signatures and errors, and (:help :topic <topic>) for staging, txn, batch, receipts, and errors. Example: asl '(:read :file \\\"src/app.py\\\" :symbol \\\"greet\\\") (:edit :file \\\"src/app.py\\\" :old \\\"return 1\\\" :new \\\"return 2\\\") (:check :file \\\"src/app.py\\\") (:flush)'.\"\n  :topics (\n    (:topic :name :staging :text \"Operations edit, write, and fix with :apply stage changes in a buffer on disk outside the working tree: .asl/vfs, or ~/.cache/asl/vfs/<hash> for a workspace without .asl; each ASL_SESSION has its own buffer, and without ASL_SESSION the workspace shares one. The buffer persists across calls until flush or discard, so a later bare (:flush) writes changes staged earlier. Operation diff shows staged changes against disk; check and test run against staged content. Operation flush writes every staged file atomically (fsync and rename) and refuses with ERR_STALE_BASE a file whose disk content changed since it was staged. Operation discard drops staged changes without touching disk. (:txn) stages, gates and flushes in one call.\" :examples (\n      \"(:diff)\"\n    ))\n    (:topic :name :txn :text \"Transaction atomicity across file edits and validation gates. The (:txn :owns (<path> ...) <form> ...) form executes nested edits and gates. All touched targets must resolve inside declared :owns boundaries. If any nested step fails or is rejected, all modifications are restored to their pre-transaction state. If all nested steps succeed, modifications are flushed atomically to disk.\" :examples (\n      \"(:txn :owns (\\\"asl/grammar\\\") (:check :file \\\"asl/grammar/rules.asn\\\"))\"\n    ))\n    (:topic :name :batch :text \"Multiple ASN forms execute in one call via asl '(:form1 ...) (:form2 ...)'. Forms execute in input order; independent read-only forms run concurrently. Ordered execution with short-circuit on first failure is requested with (:batch :seq true ...). A mutation followed by flush also short-circuits on failure so invalid staged changes never reach disk.\" :examples (\n      \"(:batch :seq true (:tools) (:diff))\"\n    ))\n    (:topic :name :receipts :text \"Every executed operation yields a structured ASN receipt. A single form prints an unwrapped receipt; multiple forms print (:batch <receipt1> <receipt2> ...). Receipts use Dyck-1 balanced parentheses and camelCase keys. Successful steps omit redundant ok status and item counts; rejected steps carry :error with an uppercase code, human-readable :message, and contextual fields.\" :examples (\n      \"(:read :file \\\"asl/grammar/rules.asn\\\" :limit 5)\"\n    ))\n    (:topic :name :errors :text \"Failures produce predictable uppercase error codes under :error in rejected step receipts. Common codes include ERR_MISSING_ARG (required parameter absent), ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND (target path does not exist in workspace), ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION (path escapes repository root), ERR_NO_MATCH (old string not found), ERR_AMBIGUOUS (multiple matches without :all true), ERR_UNBALANCED (delimiter mismatch), ERR_SYNTAX (language syntax invalid), ERR_OWNS (target outside transaction owns).\" :examples (\n      \"(:read :file \\\"missing.txt\\\")\"\n    ))\n    (:topic :name :language :text \"An ASL file is a module header, then items starting in column 0: (module ws/name :d \\\"doc\\\" :x [exported names] :i [(other/module :a alias)]). Imports name the module a file declares, not its path. A function is a bare line, fn name a: Int64 b: String -> Bool, with its body indented below; that line is not a form, so the body closes only its own parentheses. Each bracket kind pairs exactly: ( ) forms, [ ] lists, { } records. enum Shape (circle r: Int64) (square side: Int64) makes positional constructors, taken apart by (mt s ((circle r) ...) ((square a) ...)); patterns nest one level. (let [(a 1) (b (+ a 1))] body) binds in sequence; (fn [x] body) is a value; cond ends with (else v). Conditions, and, or, not and assert take only true or false. Int and Float never mix; overflow and division by zero trap. There is no nil, exception or try: listHead, listTail, listGet, listSlice, stringSlice and mapGet return (some v) or (none), failures are (err e), unwrapped by mt, optionOr or resultOr. Builtins are camelCase like user names, predicates end in ?: listLength, stringContains?, some?; len and head do not exist; + is not a value. A test exports runTests, returning true after at least one (assert cond \\\"msg\\\") or refute. The stage-0 host asl/host/out/asl-host enforces all this before running, and (:test), (:check), asl test and asl check of an .asl file and asl eval run on it (asl eval prints a keyword-headed form back as ASN data); a bare asl test or asl check sweeps every discovered suite or tracked file on it, and the lenient asl-core runner is retired.\" :tools \"After an ASL edit run asl/host/out/asl-host check FILE, then test FILE: exit 0 and the executed assert count are the evidence; a test is (module ws/t :x [runTests]) with fn runTests -> Bool ending true after (assert c); asl run FILE runs a program; asl '(:help :builtin stringTo)' lists builtins by name, else by doc, with types.\" :examples (\n      \"(:read :file \\\"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\\\" :limit 20)\"\n    ))\n  )\n  :entries (\n    (:op :tools\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Print the operation registry.\"\n      :form \"(:tools)\"\n      :params ()\n      :examples (\n        \"(:tools)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_UNIMPLEMENTED)\n      :related (help)\n      :doc \"Introspect active agent tool schemas and operational signatures.\")\n\n    (:op :help\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Show help for an op, a topic, or the ASL builtins whose name contains a text.\"\n      :form \"(:help :op <name>) | (:help :topic <topic>) | (:help :builtin <text>) | (:tools :op <name>)\"\n      :params (\n        (:op :type sym :default :read :note \"operation name to describe\")\n        (:topic :type sym :default :staging :note \"topic name to explain\")\n        (:builtin :type str :note \"text a builtin name contains, as in stringTo; when no name holds it, builtins whose doc holds its words (parse-int finds stringToInt64); answers with name, type and doc from asl/prelude/prelude.asn\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:tools :op \\\"read\\\")\"\n        \"(:help :builtin \\\"stringTo\\\")\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_UNKNOWN_SYMBOL ERR_UNIMPLEMENTED)\n      :related (tools)\n      :doc \"Display documentation, signatures, parameters, examples, and error codes for ops and topics.\")\n\n    (:op :manage\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:action :type sym :req true :note \"action: spawn poll tail kill list\")\n        (:id :type str :default \"\" :note \"task identifier\")\n        (:cmd :type str :default \"\" :note \"command string to execute\")\n        (:lines :type int :default 10 :note \"log line count for tail\")\n        (:timeoutMs :type int :default 30000 :note \"execution timeout in milliseconds\")\n      )\n      :actions (:spawn :poll :tail :kill :list)\n      :doc \"APM engine process supervision, streaming logs, and session lifecycle. Replaces host manage_task.\")\n\n    (:op :engine\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:action :type sym :req true :note \"action: status ping start stop restart\")\n        (:scope :type sym :default :workspace :note \"scope: workspace or system\")\n        (:force :type bool :default false :note \"force engine restart\")\n      )\n      :actions (:status :ping :start :stop :restart)\n      :scopes (:workspace :system)\n      :doc \"Resident ASL engine runtime management, scope isolation, socket status, liveness ping, and graceful restart/termination via RPC.\")\n\n    (:op :lens\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :default \"\" :note \"target file to evaluate\")\n        (:target :type str :default \"workspace\" :note \"target scope or path\")\n        (:lenses :type forms :default (:invariants) :note \"list of audit lenses to evaluate\")\n        (:profile :type sym :default :freeTier :note \"execution profile: freeTier frontier codexLuna\")\n      )\n      :lenses (:all :invariants :teleology :semantics :gates :triMap :grading :astAddressing :ramTxn :foreign :limitCycle :workspaceIsolation :dyck1Purity :tokenEconomics)\n      :profiles (:freeTier :frontier :codexLuna)\n      :doc \"Execute a multi-lens audit across 13 canonical inquiry lenses returning structured ASN report.\")\n\n    (:op :agent\n      :scope toolchain\n      :brief \"(:agent :task t [:root dir] [:owns (paths)] [:gates (commands)] [:intent i]) hands a task to Leon, the asl agent loop, which edits inside :root (default the calling repo), narrowed by :owns, and runs the gates\"\n      :form \"(:agent :task <str> ...)\"\n      :params (\n        (:answer :type str :default \"\")\n        (:backend :type str :default \"agy\")\n        (:base :type str :default \"\" :note \"rev gitDiff compares to\")\n        (:budget :type int :default 3000)\n        (:contextFile :type str :default \"\")\n        (:contextTokens :type int)\n        (:dryRun :type bool :default false)\n        (:gates :type forms :default ())\n        (:gateTimeout :type int)\n        (:intent :type sym)\n        (:model :type str :default \"\")\n        (:owns :type forms :default () :note \"narrows :root\")\n        (:plan :type bool :default false)\n        (:queueTimeout :type int :default 1200 :note \"seconds, outside timeout\")\n        (:resume :type str :default \"\")\n        (:root :type str)\n        (:task :type str :req true)\n        (:timeout :type int :default 600 :note \"execution seconds\")\n        (:wallBudget :type int)\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:agent :task \\\"Survey the parser\\\")\"\n        \"(:agent :task \\\"Fix the failing check\\\" :owns (\\\"src\\\") :gates (\\\"asl check\\\"))\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_UNKNOWN_ARG ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_CONTEXT_FILE ERR_BACKEND ERR_OWNS ERR_EFFECT_UNDECLARED ERR_PARSE ERR_NO_REPLY ERR_VENDOR ERR_GATEWAY_OFFLINE)\n      :doc \"Leon loop. Receipt: status session journal findings gates queueWaitSec execSec; exit 1 failed or escalated, 2 bad invocation.\")\n\n    (:op :intel\n      :scope toolchain\n      :brief \"(:intel :op outline :file f) lists a file's definitions with their line ranges; :op coupling, deadcode and stubs survey the repository\"\n      :params (\n        (:op :type sym :req true :note \"suboperation: coupling impact outline query deadcode vacuity graph complexity stubs vitality trace\")\n        (:target :type str :default \"\" :note \"target symbol package or file\")\n        (:symbol :type str :default \"\" :note \"symbol name\")\n        (:file :type str :default \"\" :note \"file path\")\n        (:strict :type bool :default false :note \"strict audit mode\")\n        (:filter :type str :default \"\" :note \"graph node filter\")\n        (:symbol :type str :note \"callers, status: the symbol\")\n        (:module :type str :note \"callers: restrict to one module (Python)\")\n        (:path :type str :note \"status: a file instead of a symbol\")\n        (:spec :type str :note \"coverage: the spec file\")\n        (:id :type str :note \"coverage: one requirement id\")\n        (:limit :type int :default 20 :note \"result limit\")\n        (:module :type str :default \"\" :note \"module path filter\")\n      )\n      :ops (:coupling :impact :outline :query :deadcode :vacuity :graph :complexity :stubs :vitality :trace)\n      :doc \"Unified Code Intelligence: whole-repo call graph, execution complexity metrics, stub detection, runtime hot-path tracing, package coupling DAG, blast radius impact, dead code detection, vacuity audit, and bounded outline extraction.\")\n\n    (:op :read\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Return a symbol or bounded slice of a file.\"\n      :form \"(:read :file <path> [:symbol <sym>] [:anchor <str>] [:limit <int>] [:start <int>] [:end <int>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :req true :note \"path to file in repository\")\n        (:symbol :type str :default \"\" :note \"symbol definition to extract\")\n        (:anchor :type str :default \"\" :note \"text anchor substring\")\n        (:limit :type int :default 200 :note \"maximum line count to return\")\n        (:start :type int :default 0 :note \"starting line number for slice\")\n        (:end :type int :default 0 :note \"ending line number for slice\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:read :file \\\"asl/grammar/rules.asn\\\" :limit 10)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND ERR_SYMBOL_NOT_FOUND ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION ERR_ANCHOR_NOT_FOUND ERR_BINARY)\n      :related (query)\n      :doc \"Bounded AST symbol and slice retrieval without whole-file dumping; a binary file (NUL in the first 8 KB or a known magic) is rejected with ERR_BINARY, :bytes and :kind, never returned.\")\n\n    (:op :query\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Search code for definitions and uses of a name; :in text searches comments, docs, memories and data instead, each labelled.\"\n      :form \"(:query :text <str> [:in code|text|all] [:limit <int>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:text :type str :req true :note \"substring or symbol query text\")\n        (:in :type sym :default :code :note \"code: definitions confirmed against the symbol index, then code lines where the text is code, and a :text count of what else matched; text: sections :comment (comments and strings in code) :doc :memory :data; all: both\")\n        (:limit :type int :default 20 :note \"maximum definition and hit count per section\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:query :text \\\"rules\\\" :limit 5)\"\n        \"(:query :text \\\"rules\\\" :in text)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_QUERY_FAILED)\n      :related (read observe)\n      :doc \"A mention outside code is not a use: it is counted under :text. Matching binary files are skipped, counted as :binarySkipped. Every call site of a function, through aliases and modules: (:observe :dim callers).\")\n\n    (:op :edit\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Stage a string replacement in the session buffer.\"\n      :form \"(:edit :file <path> :old <str> :new <str> [:all <bool>] [:autofix <sym>] [:force <bool>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :req true :note \"path to target file\")\n        (:old :type str :req true :note \"exact target string to replace\")\n        (:new :type str :req true :note \"replacement string\")\n        (:all :type bool :default false :note \"replace all occurrences\")\n        (:autofix :type sym :default :none :note \"structural or heuristic delimiter repair\")\n        (:force :type bool :default false :note \"stage despite balance or syntax errors\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:edit :file \\\"asl/grammar/rules.asn\\\" :old \\\"rules\\\" :new \\\"rules\\\" :all true)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND ERR_NO_MATCH ERR_AMBIGUOUS ERR_UNBALANCED)\n      :related (diff flush discard check txn)\n      :doc \"Atomic string replacement staged in the session buffer; rejected when the staged result breaks delimiter balance or syntax. :all replaces every occurrence, :autofix (true, indentation or heuristic) stages a delimiter repair, :force stages anyway.\")\n\n    (:op :write\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Stage whole-file content in the session buffer.\"\n      :form \"(:write :file <path> :content <str> [:force <bool>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :req true :note \"path to target file\")\n        (:content :type str :req true :note \"complete staged file content\")\n        (:force :type bool :default false :note \"stage despite balance or syntax errors\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:write :file \\\".asl/scratch.asn\\\" :content \\\"(:scratch true)\\\" :force true)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION ERR_IS_DIRECTORY ERR_UNBALANCED ERR_WRITE_FAILED)\n      :related (edit diff flush discard)\n      :doc \"Stage whole-file content in the session buffer, validated like edit; only flush touches disk.\")\n\n    (:op :tree\n      :scope toolchain\n      :form \"(:tree [:path <path>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:path :type str :default \".\" :note \"directory path to scan\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:tree :path \\\".\\\")\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_PATH_NOT_FOUND ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION)\n      :related (read query)\n      :doc \"Count files and directories under :path inside the workspace.\")\n\n    (:op :observe\n      :scope toolchain\n      :form \"(:observe :dim <tokenCost|memory|session|callers|status|coverage> [:scope p] [:limit n] [:symbol s] [:module m] [:path p] [:spec p] [:id r])\"\n      :params (\n        (:dim :type sym :req true :note \"callers: call sites of :symbol with path:line and kind, :possible, :excluded decoys; status: stub, callers, executing tests of :symbol or :path; coverage: :spec requirements implemented/tested; tokenCost: tokens by kind; memory: .asl/mem ledger sizes; session: agent sessions and :overlaps\")\n        (:scope :type str :default \".\" :note \"tokenCost: tracked files under this path\")\n        (:limit :type int :default 20 :note \"tokenCost :top or sessions shown, rest in :more; 1-100; receipt < 4096 bytes\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:observe :dim callers :symbol \\\"Cache.fetch\\\")\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_UNKNOWN_DIM ERR_NO_ENCODER ERR_BAD_ARG ERR_PATH_NOT_FOUND ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION ERR_EXEC_FAILED)\n      :doc \"Read-only workspace facts; an unknown :dim lists :nearest.\")\n\n    (:op :diff\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Show staged changes against disk.\"\n      :form \"(:diff [:file <path>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :default \"\" :note \"optional path to inspect; defaults to all staged\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:diff)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION)\n      :related (edit write flush discard)\n      :doc \"Show staged changes in the session buffer against disk.\")\n\n    (:op :flush\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Write all staged changes to disk atomically.\"\n      :form \"(:flush [:file <path>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :default \"\" :note \"optional path to persist; defaults to all staged\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:flush)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION ERR_NOT_STAGED ERR_SYNTAX_MALFORMATION ERR_STALE_BASE ERR_WRITE_FAILED)\n      :related (diff discard edit txn)\n      :doc \"Write all staged changes of the session buffer to disk atomically (fsync and rename); ERR_STALE_BASE when disk changed since staging.\")\n\n    (:op :discard\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Drop all staged changes.\"\n      :form \"(:discard [:file <path>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :default \"\" :note \"optional path to discard; defaults to all staged\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:discard)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION)\n      :related (diff flush edit)\n      :doc \"Drop all staged changes of the session buffer without touching disk.\")\n\n    (:op :check\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Check a file: delimiter balance, then for an .asl file the stage-0 host check on staged content.\"\n      :form \"(:check [:file <path>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :default \"\" :note \"file to verify; defaults to workspace check\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:check :file \\\"asl/grammar/rules.asn\\\")\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION ERR_SYNTAX ERR_UNBALANCED_DELIMITERS ERR_CHECK_FAILED ERR_HOST_ABSENT ERR_WORKSPACE_CHECK_FAILED)\n      :related (test fix edit)\n      :doc \"Verify delimiter balance of an ASL or ASN file, or run a local syntax checker on a foreign one. A balanced .asl file then goes to asl/host/out/asl-host check on the content the next flush would write, which resolves imports and names and checks arity; its exit is :checkerExit and its diagnostics come back in :message. Without :file it runs asl check over the workspace: balance of every tracked ASL and ASN file and asl/host/out/asl-host check of each .asl.\")\n\n    (:op :test\n      :scope asl\n      :public \"Run an ASL test file on the stage-0 host against staged content.\"\n      :form \"(:test :file <path>)\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :req true :note \"path to ASL test file to execute\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:test :file \\\"asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/readerTest.asl\\\")\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_TEST_FAILED ERR_VACUOUS_PASS ERR_HOST_ABSENT ERR_EXEC_FAILED)\n      :related (check fix)\n      :doc \"Run asl/host/out/asl-host test on the file as the next flush would write it: an unknown name is an error, assert takes only true or false, and runTests must return true. It passes only with a positive executed :assertCount; a failure carries the host's :exit, the asserts run before it, and its diagnostics.\")\n\n    (:op :fix\n      :scope asl\n      :public \"Propose or stage minimal delimiter repair.\"\n      :form \"(:fix :file <path> [:apply <sym>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :req true :note \"path to ASL or ASN file to balance\")\n        (:apply :type sym :default :none :note \"stage proposed repair (:true, :indentation, :heuristic)\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:fix :file \\\"asl/grammar/rules.asn\\\")\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND ERR_UNSUPPORTED_LANGUAGE ERR_AMBIGUOUS_REPAIR ERR_UNREPAIRABLE)\n      :related (check test edit)\n      :doc \"Propose, or with :apply stage, the minimal delimiter repair of an ASL/ASN file when it is structurally unique; an indentation tie-break is staged only with :apply :indentation.\")\n\n    (:op :txn\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Run nested edits and gates atomically inside owns.\"\n      :form \"(:txn :owns (<path> ...) <form> ...)\"\n      :params (\n        (:owns :type forms :req true :note \"path prefixes permitted to mutate\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:txn :owns (\\\"asl/grammar\\\") (:check :file \\\"asl/grammar/rules.asn\\\"))\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_OWNS ERR_TXN_FORBIDDEN ERR_TXN_ABORTED ERR_TXN_FLUSH_FAILED)\n      :related (edit check flush discard)\n      :doc \"Stage nested edits inside :owns, run nested gates on staged content, flush only if all pass, else restore.\")\n\n    (:op :audit\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:subcmd :type sym :default :consistency :note \"subcommand to audit\")\n      )\n      :subcmds (:consistency :gates :coupling :closure :foreign :steps :deadcode :vacuity :sweep :graph :complexity :stubs :vitality :trace :all :full)\n      :doc \"Run systemic monorepo audit across declared dimensions including whole-repo sweep, dead code, test vacuity, stub detection, runtime tracing, and master system vitality.\")\n\n    (:op :crawl\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:url :type str :req true :note \"target URL to crawl\")\n        (:mode :type sym :default :auto :note \"crawler mode: auto staticHttp patchright\")\n        (:distill :type sym :default :asn :note \"distillation format: asn text raw\")\n      )\n      :doc \"Crawl target web page and distill DOM to pure Dyck-1 ASN without noise.\")\n\n    (:op :search\n      :scope toolchain\n      :brief \"(:search :query q [:limit n]) returns web results with a short answer\"\n      :params (\n        (:query :type str :req true :note \"search query string\")\n        (:limit :type int :default 3 :note \"maximum results to return\")\n      )\n      :doc \"Cognitive web search with provider cascading and direct fallback.\")\n\n    (:op :research\n      :scope toolchain\n      :brief \"(:research :topic t [:depth :flash|:deep|:exhaustive]) researches t on the web and returns a report whose facts carry their sources and a verification status\"\n      :params (\n        (:topic :type str :req true :note \"research topic inquiry\")\n        (:depth :type sym :default :flash :note \"one of :flash (3 results, gateway flash), :deep (5 results, gateway targeted), :exhaustive (5 results plus an adversarial search, gateway matrix); another value is rejected\")\n      )\n      :doc \"Web research through the gateway: the research route of its profile extracts facts; a report is :verified only when facts with source urls pass verification, else :unverified, :noEvidence or :failed with a :reason.\")\n\n    (:op :doctor\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params ()\n      :doc \"Audit measured capabilities and substrate invariants.\")\n\n    (:op :note\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:action :type sym :default :list :note \"action: list query write\")\n        (:kind :type sym :default :observation :note \"note category\")\n        (:scope :type sym :default :workspace :note \"scope tag\")\n        (:date :type str :default \"\" :note \"observation date\")\n        (:claim :type str :default \"\" :note \"claim or note content\")\n      )\n      :doc \"Record or query working memory observations in pure ASN.\")\n\n    (:op :target\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:name :type sym :default :list :note \"target generator name\")\n        (:file :type str :default \"\" :note \"target file path\")\n      )\n      :doc \"Compile ASL to standalone target code or synchronize distribution artifacts (sh, ps1, cmd, distrib, c, go, llvm, py, rs, swift, wat).\")\n\n    (:op :pack\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:target :type str :default \"all\" :note \"target platform architecture\")\n        (:quick :type bool :default false :note \"skip packaging archives\")\n        (:dist :type bool :default false :note \"build distribution bundles\")\n        (:install :type bool :default false :note \"install compiled binary\")\n        (:skipGates :type bool :default false :note \"skip verification gates\")\n        (:self :type bool :default false :note \"build host-only binary\")\n      )\n      :doc \"Assemble native self-hosted LLVM binary, audit verification gates, and package target distribution bundles (darwin-arm64, linux-x64, wasm).\")\n  ))\n")
(:file :tree "tc1" :path "asl/packages/asl-checker/src/types.asl" :text "(module asl-checker/types :x [Type Diagnostic resolveTypeAlias unorderedType? intRangeBounds preludeUnionCases isNumericType? isIntegralType? builtinSig parseTypeStr showTypes showType collectTvars])\n\n(enum Type (:c tyCon [(name String) (args (List Type)) (mod (Option String)) (shown (Option String))] \"A nominal or constructed type\") (:c tyVar [(id Int64) (kind String)] \"A type variable metavariable: any, num, or int\") (:c tyFun [(params (List Type)) (ret Type)] \"A function type\"))\n\n(schema Diagnostic (:f code String) (:f message String) (:f msg String) (:f line Int64) (:f col Int64) (:f path String))\n\nfn resolveTypeAlias name: String -> String\n  (cond ((= name \"Bool\") \"Bool\") ((= name \"F32\") \"Float64\") ((= name \"F64\") \"Float64\") ((= name \"Float\") \"Float64\") ((= name \"I32\") \"Int32\") ((= name \"I64\") \"Int64\") ((= name \"Int\") \"Int64\") ((= name \"Num\") \"Float64\") ((= name \"Str\") \"String\") ((= name \"Unit\") \"Unit\") ((= name \"Bytes\") \"Bytes\") (else name))\n\nfn unorderedType? name: String -> Bool\n  (or (= name \"Float64\") (= name \"IoError\"))\n\nfn intRangeBounds name: String -> (Option (Pair Int64 Int64))\n  (cond ((= name \"Int32\") (some (pair -2147483648 2147483647))) ((= name \"Int64\") (some (pair -9223372036854775808 9223372036854775807))) (else (none)))\n\nfn preludeUnionCases caseName: String -> (Option String)\n  (cond ((= caseName \"alreadyExists\") (some \"IoError\")) ((= caseName \"interrupted\") (some \"IoError\")) ((= caseName \"invalidPath\") (some \"IoError\")) ((= caseName \"notFound\") (some \"IoError\")) ((= caseName \"other\") (some \"IoError\")) ((= caseName \"permissionDenied\") (some \"IoError\")) ((= caseName \"some\") (some \"Option\")) ((= caseName \"none\") (some \"Option\")) ((= caseName \"ok\") (some \"Result\")) ((= caseName \"err\") (some \"Result\")) ((= caseName \"list\") (some \"List\")) ((= caseName \"cons\") (some \"List\")) (else (none)))\n\nfn isNumericType? name: String -> Bool\n  (or (= name \"Int32\") (or (= name \"Int64\") (= name \"Float64\")))\n\nfn isIntegralType? name: String -> Bool\n  (or (= name \"Int32\") (= name \"Int64\"))\n\nfn sigFn params: (List String) ret: String -> (Option (Pair (List String) (Pair Bool String)))\n  (some (pair params (pair false ret)))\n\nfn sigVar params: (List String) ret: String -> (Option (Pair (List String) (Pair Bool String)))\n  (some (pair params (pair true ret)))\n\nfn numBinopSig -> (Option (Pair (List String) (Pair Bool String)))\n  (sigFn (list \"N\" \"N\") \"N\")\n\nfn cmpBinopSig -> (Option (Pair (List String) (Pair Bool String)))\n  (sigFn (list \"T\" \"T\") \"Bool\")\n\nfn ioerrorCtorSig -> (Option (Pair (List String) (Pair Bool String)))\n  (sigFn (list) \"IoError\")\n\nfn ioResultUnitSig -> (Option (Pair (List String) (Pair Bool String)))\n  (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Result Unit IoError)\")\n\nfn strPredSig -> (Option (Pair (List String) (Pair Bool String)))\n  (sigFn (list \"String\" \"String\") \"Bool\")\n\nfn listOptSig -> (Option (Pair (List String) (Pair Bool String)))\n  (sigFn (list \"(List T)\") \"(Option T)\")\n\nfn builtinSig name: String -> (Option (Pair (List String) (Pair Bool String)))\n  (cond ((or (= name \"sqrt\") (or (= name \"floor\") (or (= name \"ceil\") (= name \"round\")))) (sigFn (list \"Float64\") \"Float64\")) ((or (= name \"exp\") (or (= name \"log\") (or (= name \"log2\") (or (= name \"log10\") (or (= name \"sin\") (or (= name \"cos\") (= name \"tan\"))))))) (sigFn (list \"Float64\") \"Float64\")) ((or (= name \"pow\") (= name \"atan2\")) (sigFn (list \"Float64\" \"Float64\") \"Float64\")) ((or (= name \"!=\") (or (= name \"=\") (or (= name \"<\") (or (= name \"<=\") (or (= name \">\") (= name \">=\")))))) (cmpBinopSig)) ((or (= name \"*\") (or (= name \"+\") (or (= name \"-\") (= name \"/\")))) (numBinopSig)) ((or (= name \"abs\") (= name \"neg\")) (sigFn (list \"N\") \"N\")) ((or (= name \"alreadyExists\") (or (= name \"interrupted\") (or (= name \"invalidPath\") (or (= name \"notFound\") (or (= name \"other\") (= name \"permissionDenied\")))))) (ioerrorCtorSig)) ((= name \"and\") (sigVar (list \"Bool\") \"Bool\")) ((= name \"bytesAlloc\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\") \"Bytes\")) ((= name \"bytesLength\") (sigFn (list \"Bytes\") \"Int64\")) ((= name \"bytesGet\") (sigFn (list \"Bytes\" \"Int64\") \"Int64\")) ((= name \"bytesGetFloat64\") (sigFn (list \"Bytes\" \"Int64\") \"Float64\")) ((= name \"bytesSet\") (sigFn (list \"Bytes\" \"Int64\" \"Int64\") \"Unit\")) ((= name \"bytesSetFloat64\") (sigFn (list \"Bytes\" \"Int64\" \"Float64\") \"Unit\")) ((= name \"bytesToBase64\") (sigFn (list \"Bytes\") \"String\")) ((= name \"bytesFromBase64\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Result Bytes String)\")) ((or (= name \"checkedDiv\") (= name \"checkedMod\")) (sigFn (list \"N\" \"N\") \"(Option N)\")) ((or (= name \"eprintln\") (or (= name \"print\") (= name \"println\"))) (ioResultUnitSig)) ((= name \"dirList\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Result (List String) String)\")) ((= name \"err\") (sigFn (list \"E\") \"(Result T E)\")) ((= name \"processRun\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"ProcessOutput\")) ((= name \"nowNs\") (sigFn (list) \"Int64\")) ((= name \"monotonicNs\") (sigFn (list) \"Int64\")) ((= name \"sleepMs\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\") \"Unit\")) ((= name \"envGet\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Option String)\")) ((= name \"processSpawn\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"processWait\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\" \"Int64\") \"(Result ProcessOutput String)\")) ((= name \"fileLock\") (sigFn (list \"String\" \"Bool\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"fileLockWait\") (sigVar (list \"String\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"fileCreateExclusive\") (sigFn (list \"String\" \"String\") \"(Result Unit String)\")) ((= name \"fileLockAt\") (sigFn (list \"String\" \"String\" \"Bool\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"fileReadAt\") (sigFn (list \"String\" \"String\") \"(Result String String)\")) ((= name \"fileWriteAt\") (sigFn (list \"String\" \"String\" \"String\") \"(Result Unit String)\")) ((= name \"dirCreate\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Result Unit String)\")) ((= name \"pathRemove\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Result Unit String)\")) ((= name \"pathRename\") (sigFn (list \"String\" \"String\") \"(Result Unit String)\")) ((or (= name \"file-append\") (or (= name \"fileWrite\") (= name \"fileAppend\"))) (sigFn (list \"String\" \"String\") \"(Result Unit IoError)\")) ((= name \"fileExists?\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"Bool\")) ((= name \"fileRead\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Result String IoError)\")) ((= name \"fileStat\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Result FileStat String)\")) ((= name \"fileReadRange\") (sigFn (list \"String\" \"Int64\" \"Int64\") \"(Result Bytes String)\")) ((= name \"fileSize\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"pathCanonicalize\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Result String IoError)\")) ((= name \"filter\") (sigFn (list \"(fn [T] -> Bool)\" \"(List T)\") \"(List T)\")) ((= name \"float64ToInt64\") (sigFn (list \"Float64\") \"(Option Int64)\")) ((= name \"fold\") (sigFn (list \"(fn [B A] -> B)\" \"B\" \"(List A)\") \"B\")) ((= name \"int32ToInt64\") (sigFn (list \"Int32\") \"Int64\")) ((= name \"int64ToFloat64\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\") \"Float64\")) ((= name \"int64ToInt32\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\") \"(Option Int32)\")) ((or (= name \"err?\") (= name \"ok?\")) (sigFn (list \"(Result T E)\") \"Bool\")) ((or (= name \"none?\") (= name \"some?\")) (sigFn (list \"(Option T)\") \"Bool\")) ((= name \"list\") (sigVar (list \"T\") \"(List T)\")) ((= name \"listAppend\") (sigFn (list \"(List T)\" \"(List T)\") \"(List T)\")) ((= name \"listDrop\") (sigFn (list \"(List T)\" \"Int64\") \"(List T)\")) ((= name \"listTake\") (sigFn (list \"(List T)\" \"Int64\") \"(List T)\")) ((= name \"listAny?\") (sigFn (list \"(fn [T] -> Bool)\" \"(List T)\") \"Bool\")) ((= name \"listAll?\") (sigFn (list \"(fn [T] -> Bool)\" \"(List T)\") \"Bool\")) ((= name \"listLast\") (sigFn (list \"(List T)\") \"(Option T)\")) ((= name \"enumerate\") (sigFn (list \"(List T)\") \"(List (Pair Int64 T))\")) ((= name \"cons\") (sigFn (list \"T\" \"(List T)\") \"(List T)\")) ((= name \"listContains?\") (sigFn (list \"(List T)\" \"T\") \"Bool\")) ((= name \"listEmpty?\") (sigFn (list \"(List T)\") \"Bool\")) ((= name \"listGet\") (sigFn (list \"(List T)\" \"Int64\") \"(Option T)\")) ((or (= name \"listHead\") (or (= name \"listMax\") (= name \"listMin\"))) (listOptSig)) ((= name \"listIndexOf\") (sigFn (list \"(List T)\" \"T\") \"(Option Int64)\")) ((= name \"listLength\") (sigFn (list \"(List T)\") \"Int64\")) ((or (= name \"listReverse\") (= name \"listSort\")) (sigFn (list \"(List T)\") \"(List T)\")) ((= name \"listSlice\") (sigFn (list \"(List T)\" \"Int64\" \"Int64\") \"(Option (List T))\")) ((= name \"listSortBy\") (sigFn (list \"(fn [T] -> K)\" \"(List T)\") \"(List T)\")) ((= name \"listSum\") (sigFn (list \"(List N)\") \"N\")) ((= name \"listTail\") (sigFn (list \"(List T)\") \"(Option (List T))\")) ((= name \"map\") (sigFn (list \"(fn [A] -> B)\" \"(List A)\") \"(List B)\")) ((= name \"parMap\") (sigFn (list \"(fn [A] -> B)\" \"(List A)\" \"Int64\") \"(List B)\")) ((= name \"parFold\") (sigFn (list \"(fn [B A] -> B)\" \"(fn [B B] -> B)\" \"B\" \"(List A)\" \"Int64\") \"B\")) ((= name \"mapEmpty\") (sigFn (list) \"(Map K V)\")) ((= name \"mapFromPairs\") (sigFn (list \"(List (Pair K V))\") \"(Map K V)\")) ((= name \"mapGet\") (sigFn (list \"(Map K V)\" \"K\") \"(Option V)\")) ((= name \"mapHas?\") (sigFn (list \"(Map K V)\" \"K\") \"Bool\")) ((= name \"mapKeys\") (sigFn (list \"(Map K V)\") \"(List K)\")) ((= name \"mapPairs\") (sigFn (list \"(Map K V)\") \"(List (Pair K V))\")) ((= name \"mapRemove\") (sigFn (list \"(Map K V)\" \"K\") \"(Map K V)\")) ((= name \"mapSet\") (sigFn (list \"(Map K V)\" \"K\" \"V\") \"(Map K V)\")) ((= name \"mapSize\") (sigFn (list \"(Map K V)\") \"Int64\")) ((= name \"mapValues\") (sigFn (list \"(Map K V)\") \"(List V)\")) ((or (= name \"max\") (or (= name \"min\") (= name \"mod\"))) (numBinopSig)) ((= name \"none\") (sigFn (list) \"(Option T)\")) ((= name \"not\") (sigFn (list \"Bool\") \"Bool\")) ((= name \"ok\") (sigFn (list \"T\") \"(Result T E)\")) ((= name \"optionMap\") (sigFn (list \"(fn [A] -> B)\" \"(Option A)\") \"(Option B)\")) ((= name \"optionOr\") (sigFn (list \"(Option T)\" \"T\") \"T\")) ((= name \"optionToResult\") (sigFn (list \"(Option T)\" \"E\") \"(Result T E)\")) ((= name \"or\") (sigVar (list \"Bool\") \"Bool\")) ((= name \"pair\") (sigFn (list \"A\" \"B\") \"(Pair A B)\")) ((= name \"pairFirst\") (sigFn (list \"(Pair A B)\") \"A\")) ((= name \"pairSecond\") (sigFn (list \"(Pair A B)\") \"B\")) ((= name \"range\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\" \"Int64\") \"(List Int64)\")) ((= name \"read-all\") (sigFn (list) \"(Result String IoError)\")) ((= name \"read-line\") (sigFn (list) \"(Result (Option String) IoError)\")) ((= name \"resultMap\") (sigFn (list \"(Result A E)\" \"(fn [A] -> B)\") \"(Result B E)\")) ((= name \"resultMapErr\") (sigFn (list \"(fn [E] -> F)\" \"(Result T E)\") \"(Result T F)\")) ((= name \"resultOr\") (sigFn (list \"(Result T E)\" \"T\") \"T\")) ((= name \"resultToOption\") (sigFn (list \"(Result T E)\") \"(Option T)\")) ((= name \"some\") (sigFn (list \"T\") \"(Option T)\")) ((= name \"str\") (sigVar (list \"A\") \"String\")) ((= name \"stringChars\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(List String)\")) ((or (= name \"stringContains?\") (or (= name \"stringEndsWith?\") (= name \"stringStartsWith?\"))) (strPredSig)) ((= name \"stringEmpty?\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"Bool\")) ((= name \"stringFromFloat64\") (sigFn (list \"Float64\") \"String\")) ((= name \"stringFromInt64\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\") \"String\")) ((= name \"stringIndexOf\") (sigFn (list \"String\" \"String\") \"(Option Int64)\")) ((= name \"stringJoin\") (sigFn (list \"(List String)\" \"String\") \"String\")) ((= name \"stringLength\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"Int64\")) ((or (= name \"stringLower\") (or (= name \"stringReverse\") (or (= name \"stringTrim\") (= name \"stringUpper\")))) (sigFn (list \"String\") \"String\")) ((= name \"stringReplace\") (sigFn (list \"String\" \"String\" \"String\") \"String\")) ((= name \"stringSlice\") (sigFn (list \"String\" \"Int64\" \"Int64\") \"(Option String)\")) ((= name \"stringSplit\") (sigFn (list \"String\" \"String\") \"(List String)\")) ((= name \"stringToBytes\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"Bytes\")) ((= name \"stringToFloat64\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Option Float64)\")) ((= name \"stringToInt64\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Option Int64)\")) ((= name \"zip\") (sigFn (list \"(List A)\" \"(List B)\") \"(List (Pair A B))\")) ((= name \"trap\") (sigFn (list \"String\" \"String\") \"T\")) ((= name \"tcpListen\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"tcpConnect\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"sockAccept\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"sockLocalPort\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"unixListen\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"unixConnect\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"realPath\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Result String String)\")) ((= name \"fileReadlink\") (sigFn (list \"String\") \"(Result String String)\")) ((= name \"procExePath\") (sigFn (list) \"(Result String String)\")) ((= name \"fdRead\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\" \"Int64\") \"(Result String String)\")) ((= name \"hostVerb\") (sigFn (list \"(List String)\") \"Int64\")) ((= name \"hostSocketOpen\") (sigFn (list \"String\" \"Int64\" \"Bool\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"hostSocketBind\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\" \"String\" \"Int64\") \"(Result Bool String)\")) ((= name \"hostSocketListen\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\" \"Int64\") \"(Result Bool String)\")) ((= name \"hostSocketAccept\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"hostSocketRead\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\" \"Int64\") \"(Result String String)\")) ((= name \"hostSocketWrite\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\" \"String\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"hostSocketClose\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\") \"(Result Bool String)\")) ((= name \"hostSocketPoll\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\" \"Int64\") \"(Result String String)\")) ((= name \"hostSurfaceInit\") (sigFn (list \"String\" \"Int64\" \"Int64\") \"(Result Int64 String)\")) ((= name \"hostSurfacePresent\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\" \"String\" \"Int64\") \"(Result Bool String)\")) ((= name \"hostSurfaceResize\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\" \"Int64\" \"Int64\") \"(Result Bool String)\")) ((= name \"hostSurfacePollEvents\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\") \"(Result String String)\")) ((= name \"f64ArrayLen\") (sigFn (list \"F64Array\") \"Int64\")) ((= name \"i64ArrayLen\") (sigFn (list \"I64Array\") \"Int64\")) ((= name \"f64ArrayGet\") (sigFn (list \"F64Array\" \"Int64\") \"Float64\")) ((= name \"f64ArrayGenerate\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\" \"(fn [Int64] -> Float64)\") \"F64Array\")) ((= name \"f64ArraySlice\") (sigFn (list \"F64Array\" \"Int64\" \"Int64\") \"F64Array\")) ((= name \"dot\") (sigFn (list \"F64Array\" \"F64Array\") \"Float64\")) ((= name \"axpy\") (sigFn (list \"Float64\" \"F64Array\" \"F64Array\") \"F64Array\")) ((= name \"gemm\") (sigFn (list \"Int64\" \"Int64\" \"Int64\" \"F64Array\" \"F64Array\") \"F64Array\")) (else (none)))\nfn showTypes ts: (List Type) -> (List String)\n  (map (fn [(t Type)] -> String (showType t)) ts)\n\nfn stripFirstChar s: String -> String\n  (mt (stringSlice s 1 (stringLength s)) ((some sub) sub) ((none) s))\n\nfn showType t: Type -> String\n  (mt t ((tyVar id kind) (cond ((= kind \"num\") \"a number\") ((= kind \"int\") \"an integer\") (else \"_\"))) ((tyFun params ret) (str \"(fn [\" (stringJoin (showTypes params) \" \") \"] -> \" (showType ret) \")\")) ((tyCon name args mod shown) (let [(head (mt shown ((some rest) rest) ((none) (if (stringStartsWith? name \"#\") (stripFirstChar name) name))))] (if (listEmpty? args) head (str \"(\" head \" \" (stringJoin (showTypes args) \" \") \")\")))))\n\n(schema TypeTokState (:f toks (List String)) (:f cur String))\n\nfn flushCur toks: (List String) cur: String -> (List String)\n  (if (stringEmpty? cur) toks (cons cur toks))\n\nfn tokenizeTypeStep st: TypeTokState c: String -> TypeTokState\n  (cond ((or (= c \"(\") (or (= c \")\") (or (= c \"[\") (= c \"]\")))) (let [(toks1 (flushCur st.toks st.cur))] (TypeTokState :toks (cons c toks1) :cur \"\"))) ((or (= c \" \") (or (= c \"\\t\") (or (= c \"\\n\") (= c \"\\r\")))) (TypeTokState :toks (flushCur st.toks st.cur) :cur \"\")) (else (with st :cur (str st.cur c))))\n\nfn tokenizeTypeStr s: String -> (List String)\n  (let [(st (fold tokenizeTypeStep (TypeTokState :toks (list) :cur \"\") (stringChars s)))] (listReverse (flushCur st.toks st.cur)))\n\nfn getTypevarId name: String typevars: (List String) -> Int64\n  (mt (listIndexOf typevars name) ((some i) (+ i 1)) ((none) 1))\n\nfn makeQualPair member: String alias: (Option String) head: String -> (Pair String (Pair (Option String) (Option String)))\n  (let [(optH (some head))] (pair (resolveTypeAlias member) (pair alias optH)))\n\nfn parseConName head: String -> (Pair String (Pair (Option String) (Option String)))\n  (if (not (stringContains? head \"/\")) (pair (resolveTypeAlias head) (pair (none) (none))) (let [(parts (stringSplit head \"/\")) (alias (listGet parts 0))] (match (listGet parts 1) ((some s) (makeQualPair s alias head)) ((none) (makeQualPair head alias head)))))\n\nfn safeToksTail toks: (List String) -> (List String)\n  (if (listEmpty? toks) (list) (mt (listSlice toks 1 (listLength toks)) ((some rest) rest) ((none) (list))))\n\nfn skipDelim toks: (List String) delim: String -> (List String)\n  (mt (listHead toks) ((some str) (if (= str delim) (safeToksTail toks) toks)) ((none) toks))\n\nfn parseTypeToks toks: (List String) typevars: (List String) -> (Pair Type (List String))\n  (mt (listHead toks) ((none) (pair (tyCon \"Unit\" (list) (none) (none)) (list))) ((some s) (let [(rest (safeToksTail toks))] (if (= s \"(\") (mt (listHead rest) ((none) (pair (tyCon \"Unit\" (list) (none) (none)) (list))) ((some sSym) (let [(rest2 (safeToksTail rest))] (if (= sSym \"fn\") (let [(curToks (skipDelim rest2 \"[\")) (pRes (parseFnParams curToks typevars (list))) (params (pairFirst pRes)) (afterParams (pairSecond pRes)) (cur2 (skipDelim afterParams \"->\")) (retRes (parseTypeToks cur2 typevars)) (ret (pairFirst retRes)) (afterRet (pairSecond retRes)) (finalRem (skipDelim afterRet \")\"))] (pair (tyFun params ret) finalRem)) (let [(argsRes (parseTypeArgs rest2 typevars (list))) (args (pairFirst argsRes)) (afterArgs (pairSecond argsRes)) (conInfo (parseConName sSym)) (cName (pairFirst conInfo)) (cMod (pairFirst (pairSecond conInfo))) (cShown (pairSecond (pairSecond conInfo)))] (pair (tyCon cName args cMod cShown) afterArgs)))))) (if (listContains? typevars s) (let [(varId (getTypevarId s typevars)) (kind (if (= s \"N\") \"num\" (if (or (= s \"A\") (or (= s \"B\") (or (= s \"T\") (= s \"E\")))) \"any\" \"any\")))] (pair (tyVar varId kind) rest)) (let [(conInfo (parseConName s)) (cName (pairFirst conInfo)) (cMod (pairFirst (pairSecond conInfo))) (cShown (pairSecond (pairSecond conInfo)))] (pair (tyCon cName (list) cMod cShown) rest)))))))\n\nfn parseDelimitedTypes toks: (List String) typevars: (List String) closing: String acc: (List Type) -> (Pair (List Type) (List String))\n  (mt (listHead toks) ((none) (pair (listReverse acc) (list))) ((some str) (if (= str closing) (let [(revAcc (listReverse acc)) (remToks (safeToksTail toks))] (pair revAcc remToks)) (let [(res (parseTypeToks toks typevars))] (parseDelimitedTypes (pairSecond res) typevars closing (cons (pairFirst res) acc))))))\n\nfn parseTypeArgs toks: (List String) typevars: (List String) acc: (List Type) -> (Pair (List Type) (List String))\n  (parseDelimitedTypes toks typevars \")\" acc)\n\nfn parseFnParams toks: (List String) typevars: (List String) acc: (List Type) -> (Pair (List Type) (List String))\n  (parseDelimitedTypes toks typevars \"]\" acc)\n\nfn parseTypeStr s: String typevars: (List String) -> Type\n  (let [(toks (tokenizeTypeStr s))] (pairFirst (parseTypeToks toks typevars)))\n\nfn collectTvars params: (List String) ret: String -> (List String)\n  (let [(allStrs (cons ret params))]\n    (fold (fn [(acc (List String)) (s String)] -> (List String)\n            (fold (fn [(aacc (List String)) (w String)] -> (List String)\n                    (if (and (= (stringLength w) 1) (stringContains? \"ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ\" w))\n                      (if (listContains? aacc w) aacc (cons w aacc))\n                      aacc))\n                  acc\n                  (stringSplit (stringReplace (stringReplace (stringReplace (stringReplace s \"(\" \" \") \")\" \" \") \"[\" \" \") \"]\" \" \") \" \")))\n          (list)\n          allStrs))\n")
(:file :tree "tc1" :path "asl/prelude/prelude.asn" :text "(\n  :$comment \"The vocabulary the stage-0 host binds (asl/host/out/asl-host), as probed on 2026-09-24: the C builtin tables in asl/host/src (prelude.c, arrays.c, parquet.c), the operators and constructors compiled in, and the public fns of asl/prelude/prelude.asl, which the host loads before every module. :src names where each one is defined. tests/acceptance/r1Prelude/preludeParityTest.sh probes every :name below on the host and fails on ERR_UNKNOWN_SYMBOL. Nothing is generated from this file; asl-core (asl test, asl eval) binds a different set. Builtin names are camelCase with a trailing ? on predicates (D140 S2, S3); the hyphenated spellings were retired on 2026-09-25, tools/camelLexicon.asn maps each one to its name here, and the host answers ERR_UNKNOWN_SYMBOL for them.\"\n  :specialForms (\n    :declarations [\"module\" \"fn\" \"enum\" \"schema\"]\n    :expressions [\"fn\" \"lambda\" \"let\" \"if\" \"cond\" \"do\" \"begin\" \"mt\" \"match\" \"when\" \"unless\" \"assert\" \"refute\"]\n    :aliases (:lambda \"fn\" :begin \"do\" :match \"mt\")\n    :patterns \"The pattern of an mt arm is (ctor arg ...), a literal, _ or a bare name that binds the value; a constructor argument is a name or _, so patterns nest one level, and a list is not a pattern.\"\n  )\n  :types (\n    :$comment \"Annotation spellings. The host does not check annotations: a fn declared -> Int64 may return a String.\"\n    :primitive [\"Bool\" \"Int32\" \"Int64\" \"Float64\" \"String\" \"Unit\" \"Bytes\" \"F64Array\" \"I64Array\" \"I8Array\" \"ParquetHandle\"]\n    :constructed [\"List\" \"Option\" \"Result\" \"Pair\" \"Map\"]\n    :aliases (:Int \"Int64\" :I64 \"Int64\" :I32 \"Int32\" :F64 \"Float64\" :F32 \"Float64\" :Num \"Float64\" :Float \"Float64\" :Str \"String\")\n    :unions (:IoError [\"notFound\" \"permissionDenied\" \"alreadyExists\" \"invalidPath\" \"interrupted\" \"other\"] :Option [\"some\" \"none\"] :Result [\"ok\" \"err\"] :Pair [\"pair\"])\n  )\n  :absent (\n    :$comment \"Names earlier versions of this file declared that the host does not bind (asl-host eval '(fn [] NAME)' gives ERR_UNKNOWN_SYMBOL on 2026-09-24).\"\n    :names [\"read-line\" \"read-all\" \"file-append\" \"try\"]\n  )\n  :builtins [\n    (:name \"+\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"N N -> N\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"Sum of two Int or two Float; Int and Float never mix. Traps on Int64 overflow.\")\n    (:name \"-\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"N N -> N\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"Difference, or negation with one operand. Traps on Int64 overflow.\")\n    (:name \"*\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"N N -> N\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"Product. Traps on Int64 overflow.\")\n    (:name \"/\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"N N -> N\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"Division; Int division floors, so (/ -7 2) is -4. Traps on a zero Int divisor and on a quotient outside Int64.\")\n    (:name \"mod\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"Int64 Int64 -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"Floored remainder, so the sign follows the divisor: (mod -7 3) is 2. Int only; traps on a zero divisor.\")\n    (:name \"checkedDiv\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"N N -> (Option N)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Division, or none on a zero divisor or a quotient outside Int64.\")\n    (:name \"checkedMod\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"Int64 Int64 -> (Option Int64)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Floored remainder, or none on a zero divisor. A Float argument traps, as mod does.\")\n    (:name \"abs\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"N -> N\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Absolute value. Traps on the Int64 minimum.\")\n    (:name \"min\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"N N -> N\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Lesser of two Int or two Float. With a NaN the result depends on order: (min nan 1.0) is nan, (min 1.0 nan) is 1.0.\")\n    (:name \"max\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"N N -> N\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Greater of two Int or two Float. With a NaN the result depends on order: (max nan 1.0) is 1.0.\")\n    (:name \"sqrt\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"Float64 -> Float64\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Square root by scaled Newton steps; NaN for a negative or NaN argument, inf for inf.\")\n    (:name \"isNan?\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"Float64 -> Bool\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"True for NaN.\")\n    (:name \"isFinite?\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"Float64 -> Bool\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"False for NaN, inf and -inf.\")\n    (:name \"floatNan\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"-> Float64\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"The float NaN.\")\n    (:name \"floatInf\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"-> Float64\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Positive infinity.\")\n    (:name \"floatNegInf\" :sec \"Arithmetic\" :type \"-> Float64\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Negative infinity.\")\n    (:name \"=\" :sec \"Comparison and logic\" :type \"T T -> Bool\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"Structural equality over lists and records; comparing values of different kinds is a type error.\")\n    (:name \"==\" :sec \"Comparison and logic\" :type \"T T -> Bool\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"The same operator as =.\")\n    (:name \"!=\" :sec \"Comparison and logic\" :type \"T T -> Bool\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"Structural inequality.\")\n    (:name \"not=\" :sec \"Comparison and logic\" :type \"T T -> Bool\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"The same operator as !=.\")\n    (:name \"<\" :sec \"Comparison and logic\" :type \"T T -> Bool\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"Ordered comparison, for numbers and strings.\")\n    (:name \"<=\" :sec \"Comparison and logic\" :type \"T T -> Bool\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"Ordered comparison, for numbers and strings.\")\n    (:name \">\" :sec \"Comparison and logic\" :type \"T T -> Bool\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"Ordered comparison, for numbers and strings.\")\n    (:name \">=\" :sec \"Comparison and logic\" :type \"T T -> Bool\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"Ordered comparison, for numbers and strings.\")\n    (:name \"and\" :sec \"Comparison and logic\" :type \"Bool... -> Bool\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"Conjunction; short-circuits; takes one or more Bool operands. Any other value is a type error.\")\n    (:name \"or\" :sec \"Comparison and logic\" :type \"Bool... -> Bool\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"Disjunction; short-circuits; takes one or more Bool operands.\")\n    (:name \"not\" :sec \"Comparison and logic\" :type \"Bool -> Bool\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"Negation of a Bool.\")\n    (:name \"str\" :sec \"String\" :type \"T... -> String\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Concatenate the arguments; an Int or Float argument is rendered as text.\")\n    (:name \"stringConcat\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String String -> String\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Concatenate two strings.\")\n    (:name \"stringLength\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Length in UTF-8 bytes, so (stringLength \\\"héllo\\\") is 6.\")\n    (:name \"stringLines\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String -> (List String)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Split on \\\"\\\\n\\\"; a trailing newline gives a last empty line.\")\n    (:name \"stringRepeat\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String Int64 -> String\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"The string n times; n <= 0 gives \\\"\\\".\")\n    (:name \"stringCountChar\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String String -> Int64\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"How many characters of the string equal the one-character second argument.\")\n    (:name \"fnv1a64\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String -> Int64\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"FNV-1a 64-bit hash of the string's UTF-8 bytes, as a signed Int64.\")\n    (:name \"stringEmpty?\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String -> Bool\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"True when the string has no bytes.\")\n    (:name \"stringSlice\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String Int64 Int64 -> (Option String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Half-open byte slice, or none when out of range; a cut inside a multi-byte character splits it.\")\n    (:name \"stringIndexOf\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String String -> (Option Int64)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Byte index of the first occurrence, or none.\")\n    (:name \"stringContains?\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String String -> Bool\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"True when the substring occurs; the empty string always occurs.\")\n    (:name \"stringStartsWith?\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String String -> Bool\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"True when the string begins with the prefix.\")\n    (:name \"stringEndsWith?\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String String -> Bool\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"True when the string ends with the suffix.\")\n    (:name \"stringSplit\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String String -> (List String)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Split on a separator. An empty separator traps.\")\n    (:name \"stringJoin\" :sec \"String\" :type \"(List String) String -> String\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Join with a separator.\")\n    (:name \"stringUpper\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String -> String\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Upper case for ASCII letters; other characters are unchanged.\")\n    (:name \"stringLower\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String -> String\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Lower case for ASCII letters; other characters are unchanged.\")\n    (:name \"stringTrim\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String -> String\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Remove leading and trailing spaces, tabs, carriage returns and newlines.\")\n    (:name \"stringReverse\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String -> String\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Reverse the UTF-8 character sequence.\")\n    (:name \"stringReplace\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String String String -> String\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Replace every occurrence. An empty search string traps.\")\n    (:name \"stringChars\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String -> (List String)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"UTF-8 characters as one-character strings.\")\n    (:name \"stringFromInt64\" :sec \"String\" :type \"Int64 -> String\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Decimal rendering of an integer.\")\n    (:name \"stringFromFloat64\" :sec \"String\" :type \"Float64 -> String\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Decimal rendering of a float.\")\n    (:name \"stringToInt64\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String -> (Option Int64)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Parse an optionally signed integer, or none when it is malformed or outside Int64.\")\n    (:name \"stringToFloat64\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String -> Float64\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Parse a float; malformed input traps with ERR_PARSE.\")\n    (:name \"int32ToInt64\" :sec \"Numeric conversion\" :type \"Int32 -> Int64\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Widen.\")\n    (:name \"int64ToInt32\" :sec \"Numeric conversion\" :type \"Int64 -> (Option Int32)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Narrow, or none when out of range.\")\n    (:name \"int64ToFloat64\" :sec \"Numeric conversion\" :type \"Int64 -> Float64\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Convert to floating point.\")\n    (:name \"float64ToInt64\" :sec \"Numeric conversion\" :type \"Float64 -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Truncate toward zero; NaN, infinity and values outside Int64 trap with ERR_RANGE.\")\n    (:name \"list\" :sec \"List\" :type \"T... -> (List T)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Construct a list; [a b] is the same value.\")\n    (:name \"cons\" :sec \"List\" :type \"T (List T) -> (List T)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Prepend an element.\")\n    (:name \"listEmpty?\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) -> Bool\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"True when the list has no elements.\")\n    (:name \"listLength\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Element count.\")\n    (:name \"listGet\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) Int64 -> (Option T)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Element at an index, or none.\")\n    (:name \"listHead\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) -> (Option T)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"First element, or none.\")\n    (:name \"listTail\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) -> (Option (List T))\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"All but the first element, or none when empty.\")\n    (:name \"listAppend\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) (List T) -> (List T)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Concatenate two lists.\")\n    (:name \"listReverse\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) -> (List T)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Reverse order.\")\n    (:name \"listSlice\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) Int64 Int64 -> (Option (List T))\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Half-open slice, or none when out of range.\")\n    (:name \"listContains?\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) T -> Bool\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"True when the element occurs.\")\n    (:name \"listIndexOf\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) T -> (Option Int64)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Index of the first occurrence, or none.\")\n    (:name \"listSort\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) -> (List T)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Stable ascending merge sort; a NaN sorts last.\")\n    (:name \"listSortBy\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(fn [T] -> K) (List T) -> (List T)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Stable ascending sort by a derived key; a NaN key sorts last.\")\n    (:name \"map\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(fn [A] -> B) (List A) -> (List B)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Apply a function to every element.\")\n    (:name \"filter\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(fn [T] -> Bool) (List T) -> (List T)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Keep elements satisfying a predicate, which must return a Bool.\")\n    (:name \"fold\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(fn [B A] -> B) B (List A) -> B\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Left fold with an initial accumulator.\")\n    (:name \"range\" :sec \"List\" :type \"Int64 Int64 -> (List Int64)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Half-open integer range; empty when start is not below end.\")\n    (:name \"listTake\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) Int64 -> (List T)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"The first n elements, fewer when the list is shorter; n <= 0 gives (list).\")\n    (:name \"listDrop\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) Int64 -> (List T)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"The list without its first n elements; (list) when it is shorter.\")\n    (:name \"listLast\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) -> (Option T)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"The last element, or none for an empty list.\")\n    (:name \"listAny?\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(fn [T] -> Bool) (List T) -> Bool\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"True when the predicate holds for some element; stops at the first.\")\n    (:name \"listAll?\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(fn [T] -> Bool) (List T) -> Bool\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"True when the predicate holds for every element, so true for an empty list.\")\n    (:name \"enumerate\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) -> (List (Pair Int64 T))\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Each element paired with its index from 0.\")\n    (:name \"zip\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List A) (List B) -> (List (Pair A B))\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Pair up elements, truncating to the shorter list.\")\n    (:name \"listSum\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List N) -> N\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Sum of elements, 0 when empty. Traps on Int64 overflow.\")\n    (:name \"listMin\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) -> (Option T)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Least element, or none when empty.\")\n    (:name \"listMax\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(List T) -> (Option T)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Greatest element, or none when empty.\")\n    (:name \"partial\" :sec \"List\" :type \"(fn [A... B...] -> R) A... -> (fn [B...] -> R)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Bind leading arguments of a function.\")\n    (:name \"mapEmpty\" :sec \"Map\" :type \"-> (Map K V)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"The empty map.\")\n    (:name \"mapGet\" :sec \"Map\" :type \"(Map K V) K -> (Option V)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Value for a key, or none.\")\n    (:name \"mapSet\" :sec \"Map\" :type \"(Map K V) K V -> (Map K V)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Map with the key bound to the value; entries stay ordered by key.\")\n    (:name \"mapRemove\" :sec \"Map\" :type \"(Map K V) K -> (Map K V)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Map without the key.\")\n    (:name \"mapHas?\" :sec \"Map\" :type \"(Map K V) K -> Bool\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"True when the key is present.\")\n    (:name \"mapSize\" :sec \"Map\" :type \"(Map K V) -> Int64\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Number of entries.\")\n    (:name \"mapKeys\" :sec \"Map\" :type \"(Map K V) -> (List K)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Keys, sorted.\")\n    (:name \"mapValues\" :sec \"Map\" :type \"(Map K V) -> (List V)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Values, ordered by sorted key.\")\n    (:name \"mapPairs\" :sec \"Map\" :type \"(Map K V) -> (List (Pair K V))\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Entries as pairs, ordered by sorted key.\")\n    (:name \"mapFromPairs\" :sec \"Map\" :type \"(List (Pair K V)) -> (Map K V)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Build from pairs; later entries win.\")\n    (:name \"some\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"T -> (Option T)\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"A present value (constructor).\")\n    (:name \"none\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"-> (Option T)\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"An absent value (constructor).\")\n    (:name \"ok\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"T -> (Result T E)\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"A successful result (constructor).\")\n    (:name \"err\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"E -> (Result T E)\" :src \"asl/host/src/compile.c\"\n      :doc \"A failed result (constructor).\")\n    (:name \"pair\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"A B -> (Pair A B)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Construct a pair, taken apart with (mt p ((pair a b) ...)); a pair has no .-first field.\")\n    (:name \"pairFirst\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"(Pair A B) -> A\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"First component of a pair.\")\n    (:name \"pairSecond\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"(Pair A B) -> B\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Second component of a pair.\")\n    (:name \"some?\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"(Option T) -> Bool\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"True when a value is present.\")\n    (:name \"none?\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"(Option T) -> Bool\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"True when no value is present.\")\n    (:name \"ok?\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"(Result T E) -> Bool\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"True when the result succeeded.\")\n    (:name \"err?\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"(Result T E) -> Bool\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"True when the result failed.\")\n    (:name \"optionOr\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"(Option T) T -> T\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"The value, or a fallback when absent.\")\n    (:name \"resultOr\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"(Result T E) T -> T\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"The value, or a fallback on failure.\")\n    (:name \"optionMap\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"(fn [A] -> B) (Option A) -> (Option B)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Transform a present value.\")\n    (:name \"resultMap\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"(Result A E) (fn [A] -> B) -> (Result B E)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Transform a successful value. The Result comes first, unlike optionMap and resultMapErr.\")\n    (:name \"resultMapErr\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"(fn [E] -> F) (Result T E) -> (Result T F)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Transform a failure value.\")\n    (:name \"optionToResult\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"(Option T) E -> (Result T E)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Absent becomes the given failure.\")\n    (:name \"resultToOption\" :sec \"Option, Result, Pair\" :type \"(Result T E) -> (Option T)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Failure becomes absence.\")\n    (:name \"notFound\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"-> IoError\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"The not found failure (constructor).\")\n    (:name \"permissionDenied\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"-> IoError\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"The permission denied failure (constructor).\")\n    (:name \"alreadyExists\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"-> IoError\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"The already exists failure (constructor).\")\n    (:name \"invalidPath\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"-> IoError\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"The invalid path failure (constructor).\")\n    (:name \"interrupted\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"-> IoError\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"The interrupted failure (constructor).\")\n    (:name \"other\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"-> IoError\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"The other failure (constructor).\")\n    (:name \"fileExists?\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String -> Bool\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\" :effect true\n      :doc \"True when fileStat succeeds on the path (a file or a directory).\")\n    (:name \"print\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"T... -> Unit\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Write the arguments to standard output, separated by spaces, with no trailing newline.\")\n    (:name \"println\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"T... -> Unit\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Write the arguments to standard output, separated by spaces, then a newline.\")\n    (:name \"eprintln\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"T... -> Unit\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Write the arguments to standard error, separated by spaces, then a newline.\")\n    (:name \"fileRead\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String -> (Result String IoError)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Read a whole file as text; the failure is the IoError case of the host message, e.g. (err (notFound)).\")\n    (:name \"fileReadString\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String -> (Result String String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Read a whole file as text. Every host IO failure is the message \\\"KIND: PATH: reason\\\", KIND an IoError case from errno, as in \\\"notFound: /x: No such file or directory\\\".\")\n    (:name \"fileReadBytes\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String -> (Result Bytes String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Read a whole file as bytes; the failure is a \\\"KIND: PATH: reason\\\" message.\")\n    (:name \"fileReadRange\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String Int64 Int64 -> (Result Bytes String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Read length bytes starting at offset from path via pread; window past the end returns bytes up to the end; negative offset or length or missing file returns err.\")\n    (:name \"fileSize\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String -> (Result Int64 String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"File size in bytes via stat; the failure is a \\\"KIND: PATH: reason\\\" message.\")\n    (:name \"fileWrite\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String (String|Bytes) -> (Result Unit String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Create or truncate a file and write the text or bytes; the failure is a \\\"KIND: PATH: reason\\\" message.\")\n    (:name \"dirList\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String -> (Result (List String) String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Entry names of a directory without . and .., sorted bytewise; the failure is a \\\"KIND: PATH: reason\\\" message.\")\n    (:name \"fileStat\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String -> (Result FileStat String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"stat of a path as {:isFile Bool :isDir Bool :size Int64 :mtime Int64 :mode Int64}; the failure is a \\\"KIND: PATH: reason\\\" message.\")\n    (:name \"processRun\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String -> ProcessOutput\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Run a command with /bin/sh -c and wait: {:exitCode Int64 :stdout String :stderr String}; a child killed by signal N exits 128+N. Failing to start it (pipe, fork) traps with ERR_IO.\")\n    (:name \"nowNs\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"-> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (CLOCK_REALTIME).\")\n    (:name \"monotonicNs\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"-> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Nanoseconds of monotonic time since an unspecified starting point (CLOCK_MONOTONIC).\")\n    (:name \"sleepMs\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"Int64 -> Unit\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Sleep for ms milliseconds (nanosleep, resumed after EINTR). A negative ms traps with ERR_RANGE.\")\n    (:name \"envGet\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String -> (Option String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Read an environment variable by name: (some val) or (none).\")\n    (:name \"processSpawn\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String -> (Result Int64 String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Start /bin/sh -c cmd with stdout and stderr redirected, returning a handle id.\")\n    (:name \"processWait\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"Int64 Int64 -> (Result ProcessOutput String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Wait up to timeoutMs (0 = no limit) for handle: (ok {:exitCode ... :stdout ... :stderr ...}); on timeout kills process group and returns exitCode 124.\")\n    (:name \"fileCreateExclusive\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String String -> (Result Unit String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Create a file exclusively (O_CREAT|O_EXCL) and write content; returns err \\\"exists\\\" if file already exists.\")\n    (:name \"dirCreate\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String -> (Result Unit String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Create directory and any missing parents (mkdir -p semantics); ok if dir exists, err if a file exists there.\")\n    (:name \"pathRemove\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String -> (Result Unit String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Remove a file or directory tree recursively without following symlinks out of it.\")\n    (:name \"pathRename\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String String -> (Result Unit String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Rename from to (rename(2)).\")\n    (:name \"realPath\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String -> (Result String String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Resolve a path with realpath; the failure is a \\\"KIND: PATH: reason\\\" message.\")\n    (:name \"pathCanonicalize\" :sec \"I/O\" :type \"String -> (Result String IoError)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Resolve a path with realpath; the failure is the IoError case, e.g. (err (notFound)).\")\n    (:name \"bytesLength\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"Bytes -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Byte count.\")\n    (:name \"bytesAlloc\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"Int64 -> Bytes\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"n zero bytes; a negative n traps with ERR_RANGE.\")\n    (:name \"bytesGet\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"Bytes Int64 -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"The byte at an index, 0..255; an index outside the bytes traps with ERR_RANGE.\")\n    (:name \"bytesSet\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"Bytes Int64 Int64 -> Unit\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Overwrite the byte at an index in place; an index outside the bytes or a value outside 0..255 traps with ERR_RANGE.\")\n    (:name \"bytesGetFloat64\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"Bytes Int64 -> Float64\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"The native-endian Float64 in 8-byte slot i; a slot outside the bytes traps with ERR_RANGE.\")\n    (:name \"bytesSetFloat64\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"Bytes Int64 Float64 -> Unit\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Overwrite 8-byte slot i in place; a slot outside the bytes traps with ERR_RANGE, an Int value with ERR_TYPE.\")\n    (:name \"stringToBytes\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"String -> Bytes\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"The UTF-8 bytes of a string. The one string primitive past stringLength, stringSlice and stringConcat; charCode and fnv1a64 derive from it.\")\n    (:name \"bytesToBase64\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"Bytes -> String\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"RFC 4648 base64 with = padding.\")\n    (:name \"bytesFromBase64\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"String -> (Result Bytes String)\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Decode padded RFC 4648 base64; a character outside the alphabet, misplaced padding or a length not a multiple of 4 is an err.\")\n    (:name \"charCode\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"String -> Int64\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Unicode code point of the first character, so (charCode \\\"é\\\") is 233; the empty string traps.\")\n    (:name \"bitAnd\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"Int64 Int64 -> Int64\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Bitwise and on two's complement Int64.\")\n    (:name \"bitOr\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"Int64 Int64 -> Int64\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Bitwise or on two's complement Int64.\")\n    (:name \"bitXor\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"Int64 Int64 -> Int64\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Bitwise exclusive or on two's complement Int64.\")\n    (:name \"bitNot\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"Int64 -> Int64\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Bitwise complement, (- -1 x).\")\n    (:name \"popcount64\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"Int64 -> Int64\" :src \"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\"\n      :doc \"Number of one bits in the two's complement Int64, so (popcount64 -1) is 64.\")\n    (:name \"bytesSha256\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"Bytes -> String\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"SHA-256 digest as 64 lower-case hex characters.\")\n    (:name \"zstdDecompress\" :sec \"Bytes\" :type \"Bytes -> (Result Bytes String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/prelude.c\"\n      :doc \"Decompress a zstd frame; the failure is a message.\")\n    (:name \"f64ArrayLen\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"F64Array -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Element count.\")\n    (:name \"f64ArrayGet\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"F64Array Int64 -> Float64\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Element at an index; an index outside the array traps with ERR_RANGE.\")\n    (:name \"f64ArraySlice\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"F64Array Int64 Int64 -> F64Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Half-open copy; bounds outside the array trap with ERR_RANGE.\")\n    (:name \"f64ArrayConcat\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"(List F64Array) -> F64Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Concatenate a list of arrays.\")\n    (:name \"f64ArrayGenerate\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"Int64 (fn [Int64] -> Float64) -> F64Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Array of n elements, element i from the function applied to i.\")\n    (:name \"f64ArraySum\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"F64Array -> Float64\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Neumaier-compensated sum.\")\n    (:name \"f64ArrayCountEq\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"F64Array Float64 -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Number of elements equal to the value.\")\n    (:name \"f64ArrayFold\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"(fn [B Float64] -> B) B F64Array -> B\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Left fold.\")\n    (:name \"f64ArrayScan\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"(fn [Float64 Float64] -> Float64) Float64 F64Array -> F64Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Every intermediate accumulator of a left fold, as an array.\")\n    (:name \"i64ArrayLen\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"I64Array -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Element count.\")\n    (:name \"i64ArrayGet\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"I64Array Int64 -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Element at an index; an index outside the array traps with ERR_RANGE.\")\n    (:name \"i64ArraySlice\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"I64Array Int64 Int64 -> I64Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Half-open copy; bounds outside the array trap with ERR_RANGE.\")\n    (:name \"i64ArrayConcat\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"(List I64Array) -> I64Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Concatenate a list of arrays.\")\n    (:name \"i64ArrayGenerate\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"Int64 (fn [Int64] -> Int64) -> I64Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Array of n elements, element i from the function applied to i.\")\n    (:name \"i64ArraySum\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"I64Array -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Sum; traps on Int64 overflow.\")\n    (:name \"i64ArrayCountEq\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"I64Array Int64 -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Number of elements equal to the value.\")\n    (:name \"i64ArrayFold\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"(fn [B Int64] -> B) B I64Array -> B\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Left fold. The accumulator must end as an Int.\")\n    (:name \"i64ArrayScan\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"(fn [Int64 Int64] -> Int64) Int64 I64Array -> I64Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Every intermediate accumulator of a left fold, as an array.\")\n    (:name \"i8ArrayLen\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"I8Array -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Element count.\")\n    (:name \"i8ArrayGet\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"I8Array Int64 -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Element at an index; an index outside the array traps with ERR_RANGE.\")\n    (:name \"i8ArraySlice\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"I8Array Int64 Int64 -> I8Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Half-open copy; bounds outside the array trap with ERR_RANGE.\")\n    (:name \"i8ArrayConcat\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"(List I8Array) -> I8Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Concatenate a list of arrays.\")\n    (:name \"i8ArrayGenerate\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"Int64 (fn [Int64] -> Int64) -> I8Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Array of n elements, element i from the function applied to i. An element outside -128..127 traps.\")\n    (:name \"i8ArraySum\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"I8Array -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Sum; traps on Int64 overflow.\")\n    (:name \"i8ArrayCountEq\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"I8Array Int64 -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Number of elements equal to the value.\")\n    (:name \"i8ArrayFold\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"(fn [B Int64] -> B) B I8Array -> B\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Left fold. The accumulator must end as an Int.\")\n    (:name \"i8ArrayScan\" :sec \"Arrays\" :type \"(fn [Int64 Int64] -> Int64) Int64 I8Array -> I8Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/arrays.c\"\n      :doc \"Every intermediate accumulator of a left fold, as an array.\")\n    (:name \"parquetOpen\" :sec \"Parquet\" :type \"String -> (Result ParquetHandle String)\" :src \"asl/host/src/parquet.c\" :effect true\n      :doc \"Open a Parquet file; the failure is a message.\")\n    (:name \"parquetNumRowGroups\" :sec \"Parquet\" :type \"ParquetHandle -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/parquet.c\"\n      :doc \"Row group count.\")\n    (:name \"parquetNumRows\" :sec \"Parquet\" :type \"ParquetHandle -> Int64\" :src \"asl/host/src/parquet.c\"\n      :doc \"Row count.\")\n    (:name \"parquetColumnType\" :sec \"Parquet\" :type \"ParquetHandle String -> String\" :src \"asl/host/src/parquet.c\"\n      :doc \"The column's physical type: int64, double, int8, int32 or other. An unknown column traps.\")\n    (:name \"parquetReadF64\" :sec \"Parquet\" :type \"ParquetHandle String Int64 -> F64Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/parquet.c\"\n      :doc \"A double column of one row group; a wrong type or row group traps.\")\n    (:name \"parquetReadI64\" :sec \"Parquet\" :type \"ParquetHandle String Int64 -> I64Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/parquet.c\"\n      :doc \"An int64 column of one row group; a wrong type or row group traps.\")\n    (:name \"parquetReadI8\" :sec \"Parquet\" :type \"ParquetHandle String Int64 -> I8Array\" :src \"asl/host/src/parquet.c\"\n      :doc \"An int8 column of one row group; a wrong type or row group traps.\")\n  ]\n)\n")
(:file :tree "tc1" :path "bin/asl" :text "not executable\n")
(:file :tree "tc1" :path "intel" :text "[ \"$1\" = impact ] || { echo \"intel stub: want impact, got $1\" >&2; exit 9; }\nshift\nexec /bin/sh ./impact \"$@\"\n")
(:file :tree "tc1" :path "impact" :text "i=0\nwhile [ $i -lt 50 ]; do printf 'stderr%04d ' $i >&2; i=$((i+1)); done\nexit 3\n")
(:file :tree "tcEdge" :path "asl/grammar/tools.asn" :text "(:tools :v 2\n  :topics (\n    (:topic :name :alpha :text \"Alpha (paren) topic\" :examples (\"(:x)\"))\n    (:topic :beta :text \"no name key\")\n    (:topic :name :alpha :text \"dup   alpha\n  spaced\")\n  )\n  :entries (\n    (:op :zed :scope any :public \"Zed \\\"quoted\\\" op\" :form \"(:zed)\" :params ((:path :type str :req true :note \"a \\\\ path\") (:limit :type int :default 20) (:mode :default :fast) (:flag :type bool :default true) (:list :default (a b)) (:neg :default -1 :default 7) (:plain)) :examples (\"(:zed :path \\\"x\\\")\" \"(:zed)\") :errors (ERR_A :ERR_B) :related (help :tools) :doc \"Zed doc\")\n    (:op :noparams :scope any :doc \"carries the previous compact params\")\n    (:op :asl-only :scope asl :doc \"asl scoped	doc\")\n    (:op :tc :doc \"no scope means toolchain\")\n    (:op :zed :scope any :params () :doc \"duplicate zed later\")\n    (:op :dash- :scope any :params ())\n    (:op :multi :scope   any :params ((:x)) :public \"multi\nline public\")\n    (:op :unclosed :scope any :params ((:y :type int)\n  ))\n  (:op :tail :scope any\n")
(:file :tree "tcEdge" :path "asl/prelude/prelude.asn" :text "(:prelude\n  :absent (\n    :names [\"read-line\" \"try-it\"]\n  )\n  :builtins [\n    (:name \"stringWidget\" :sec \"String\" :type \"String -> String\" :src \"x\"\n      :doc \"Widget \\\"quoted\\\" doc.\")\n    (:name \"parseInt\" :sec \"Int\" :type \"String -> Int64\"\n\n      :doc \"Parse an integer from text.\")\n    (:name \"broken\" :sec \"X\" :type \"T\" :src \"y\" :doc \"same line doc\")\n    (:name \"esc\\\\name\" :sec \"S\" :type \"T\"\n      :doc \"tab\\there\")\n  ]\n)\n")
(:file :tree "tcEmpty" :path "asl/grammar/tools.asn" :text "")
(:file :tree "tcNoPrelude" :path "asl/grammar/tools.asn" :text "(:tools :v 2 :substrate \"ASL\"\n  :doc \"Authoritative machine-readable registry of operational Pure-ASN S-expressions for autonomous agents. Agents execute operations exclusively via these forms.\"\n  :t0 \"AgentScript (asl) runs batch file operations on the git repository containing the working directory. Reach for it for targeted symbol reads instead of dumping files, definitions plus uses in one step, and atomic edits validated before disk commit. Edits and writes stage in a session buffer on disk that persists across calls; (:diff), (:check) and (:test) see staged content, (:flush) writes it, (:discard) drops it. asl exits 0 on success, 1 on rejected forms, and 2 on syntax or balance errors. Forms can also come from a file, asl -f FILE, or from stdin, asl -, with the same batch and exit codes; a heredoc with a quoted delimiter (asl - <<'ASN') passes a form holding a single quote, which asl '...' cannot. Discover operations via (:tools) for the full registry, (:help :op <name>) for signatures and errors, and (:help :topic <topic>) for staging, txn, batch, receipts, and errors. Example: asl '(:read :file \\\"src/app.py\\\" :symbol \\\"greet\\\") (:edit :file \\\"src/app.py\\\" :old \\\"return 1\\\" :new \\\"return 2\\\") (:check :file \\\"src/app.py\\\") (:flush)'.\"\n  :topics (\n    (:topic :name :staging :text \"Operations edit, write, and fix with :apply stage changes in a buffer on disk outside the working tree: .asl/vfs, or ~/.cache/asl/vfs/<hash> for a workspace without .asl; each ASL_SESSION has its own buffer, and without ASL_SESSION the workspace shares one. The buffer persists across calls until flush or discard, so a later bare (:flush) writes changes staged earlier. Operation diff shows staged changes against disk; check and test run against staged content. Operation flush writes every staged file atomically (fsync and rename) and refuses with ERR_STALE_BASE a file whose disk content changed since it was staged. Operation discard drops staged changes without touching disk. (:txn) stages, gates and flushes in one call.\" :examples (\n      \"(:diff)\"\n    ))\n    (:topic :name :txn :text \"Transaction atomicity across file edits and validation gates. The (:txn :owns (<path> ...) <form> ...) form executes nested edits and gates. All touched targets must resolve inside declared :owns boundaries. If any nested step fails or is rejected, all modifications are restored to their pre-transaction state. If all nested steps succeed, modifications are flushed atomically to disk.\" :examples (\n      \"(:txn :owns (\\\"asl/grammar\\\") (:check :file \\\"asl/grammar/rules.asn\\\"))\"\n    ))\n    (:topic :name :batch :text \"Multiple ASN forms execute in one call via asl '(:form1 ...) (:form2 ...)'. Forms execute in input order; independent read-only forms run concurrently. Ordered execution with short-circuit on first failure is requested with (:batch :seq true ...). A mutation followed by flush also short-circuits on failure so invalid staged changes never reach disk.\" :examples (\n      \"(:batch :seq true (:tools) (:diff))\"\n    ))\n    (:topic :name :receipts :text \"Every executed operation yields a structured ASN receipt. A single form prints an unwrapped receipt; multiple forms print (:batch <receipt1> <receipt2> ...). Receipts use Dyck-1 balanced parentheses and camelCase keys. Successful steps omit redundant ok status and item counts; rejected steps carry :error with an uppercase code, human-readable :message, and contextual fields.\" :examples (\n      \"(:read :file \\\"asl/grammar/rules.asn\\\" :limit 5)\"\n    ))\n    (:topic :name :errors :text \"Failures produce predictable uppercase error codes under :error in rejected step receipts. Common codes include ERR_MISSING_ARG (required parameter absent), ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND (target path does not exist in workspace), ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION (path escapes repository root), ERR_NO_MATCH (old string not found), ERR_AMBIGUOUS (multiple matches without :all true), ERR_UNBALANCED (delimiter mismatch), ERR_SYNTAX (language syntax invalid), ERR_OWNS (target outside transaction owns).\" :examples (\n      \"(:read :file \\\"missing.txt\\\")\"\n    ))\n    (:topic :name :language :text \"An ASL file is a module header, then items starting in column 0: (module ws/name :d \\\"doc\\\" :x [exported names] :i [(other/module :a alias)]). Imports name the module a file declares, not its path. A function is a bare line, fn name a: Int64 b: String -> Bool, with its body indented below; that line is not a form, so the body closes only its own parentheses. Each bracket kind pairs exactly: ( ) forms, [ ] lists, { } records. enum Shape (circle r: Int64) (square side: Int64) makes positional constructors, taken apart by (mt s ((circle r) ...) ((square a) ...)); patterns nest one level. (let [(a 1) (b (+ a 1))] body) binds in sequence; (fn [x] body) is a value; cond ends with (else v). Conditions, and, or, not and assert take only true or false. Int and Float never mix; overflow and division by zero trap. There is no nil, exception or try: listHead, listTail, listGet, listSlice, stringSlice and mapGet return (some v) or (none), failures are (err e), unwrapped by mt, optionOr or resultOr. Builtins are camelCase like user names, predicates end in ?: listLength, stringContains?, some?; len and head do not exist; + is not a value. A test exports runTests, returning true after at least one (assert cond \\\"msg\\\") or refute. The stage-0 host asl/host/out/asl-host enforces all this before running, and (:test), (:check), asl test and asl check of an .asl file and asl eval run on it (asl eval prints a keyword-headed form back as ASN data); a bare asl test or asl check sweeps every discovered suite or tracked file on it, and the lenient asl-core runner is retired.\" :tools \"After an ASL edit run asl/host/out/asl-host check FILE, then test FILE: exit 0 and the executed assert count are the evidence; a test is (module ws/t :x [runTests]) with fn runTests -> Bool ending true after (assert c); asl run FILE runs a program; asl '(:help :builtin stringTo)' lists builtins by name, else by doc, with types.\" :examples (\n      \"(:read :file \\\"asl/prelude/prelude.asl\\\" :limit 20)\"\n    ))\n  )\n  :entries (\n    (:op :tools\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Print the operation registry.\"\n      :form \"(:tools)\"\n      :params ()\n      :examples (\n        \"(:tools)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_UNIMPLEMENTED)\n      :related (help)\n      :doc \"Introspect active agent tool schemas and operational signatures.\")\n\n    (:op :help\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Show help for an op, a topic, or the ASL builtins whose name contains a text.\"\n      :form \"(:help :op <name>) | (:help :topic <topic>) | (:help :builtin <text>) | (:tools :op <name>)\"\n      :params (\n        (:op :type sym :default :read :note \"operation name to describe\")\n        (:topic :type sym :default :staging :note \"topic name to explain\")\n        (:builtin :type str :note \"text a builtin name contains, as in stringTo; when no name holds it, builtins whose doc holds its words (parse-int finds stringToInt64); answers with name, type and doc from asl/prelude/prelude.asn\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:tools :op \\\"read\\\")\"\n        \"(:help :builtin \\\"stringTo\\\")\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_UNKNOWN_SYMBOL ERR_UNIMPLEMENTED)\n      :related (tools)\n      :doc \"Display documentation, signatures, parameters, examples, and error codes for ops and topics.\")\n\n    (:op :manage\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:action :type sym :req true :note \"action: spawn poll tail kill list\")\n        (:id :type str :default \"\" :note \"task identifier\")\n        (:cmd :type str :default \"\" :note \"command string to execute\")\n        (:lines :type int :default 10 :note \"log line count for tail\")\n        (:timeoutMs :type int :default 30000 :note \"execution timeout in milliseconds\")\n      )\n      :actions (:spawn :poll :tail :kill :list)\n      :doc \"APM engine process supervision, streaming logs, and session lifecycle. Replaces host manage_task.\")\n\n    (:op :engine\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:action :type sym :req true :note \"action: status ping start stop restart\")\n        (:scope :type sym :default :workspace :note \"scope: workspace or system\")\n        (:force :type bool :default false :note \"force engine restart\")\n      )\n      :actions (:status :ping :start :stop :restart)\n      :scopes (:workspace :system)\n      :doc \"Resident ASL engine runtime management, scope isolation, socket status, liveness ping, and graceful restart/termination via RPC.\")\n\n    (:op :lens\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :default \"\" :note \"target file to evaluate\")\n        (:target :type str :default \"workspace\" :note \"target scope or path\")\n        (:lenses :type forms :default (:invariants) :note \"list of audit lenses to evaluate\")\n        (:profile :type sym :default :freeTier :note \"execution profile: freeTier frontier codexLuna\")\n      )\n      :lenses (:all :invariants :teleology :semantics :gates :triMap :grading :astAddressing :ramTxn :foreign :limitCycle :workspaceIsolation :dyck1Purity :tokenEconomics)\n      :profiles (:freeTier :frontier :codexLuna)\n      :doc \"Execute a multi-lens audit across 13 canonical inquiry lenses returning structured ASN report.\")\n\n    (:op :agent\n      :scope toolchain\n      :brief \"(:agent :task t [:root dir] [:owns (paths)] [:gates (commands)] [:intent i]) hands a task to Leon, the asl agent loop, which edits inside :root (default the calling repo), narrowed by :owns, and runs the gates\"\n      :form \"(:agent :task <str> ...)\"\n      :params (\n        (:answer :type str :default \"\")\n        (:backend :type str :default \"agy\")\n        (:base :type str :default \"\" :note \"rev gitDiff compares to\")\n        (:budget :type int :default 3000)\n        (:contextFile :type str :default \"\")\n        (:contextTokens :type int)\n        (:dryRun :type bool :default false)\n        (:gates :type forms :default ())\n        (:gateTimeout :type int)\n        (:intent :type sym)\n        (:model :type str :default \"\")\n        (:owns :type forms :default () :note \"narrows :root\")\n        (:plan :type bool :default false)\n        (:queueTimeout :type int :default 1200 :note \"seconds, outside timeout\")\n        (:resume :type str :default \"\")\n        (:root :type str)\n        (:task :type str :req true)\n        (:timeout :type int :default 600 :note \"execution seconds\")\n        (:wallBudget :type int)\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:agent :task \\\"Survey the parser\\\")\"\n        \"(:agent :task \\\"Fix the failing check\\\" :owns (\\\"src\\\") :gates (\\\"asl check\\\"))\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_UNKNOWN_ARG ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_CONTEXT_FILE ERR_BACKEND ERR_OWNS ERR_EFFECT_UNDECLARED ERR_PARSE ERR_NO_REPLY ERR_VENDOR ERR_GATEWAY_OFFLINE)\n      :doc \"Leon loop. Receipt: status session journal findings gates queueWaitSec execSec; exit 1 failed or escalated, 2 bad invocation.\")\n\n    (:op :intel\n      :scope toolchain\n      :brief \"(:intel :op outline :file f) lists a file's definitions with their line ranges; :op coupling, deadcode and stubs survey the repository\"\n      :params (\n        (:op :type sym :req true :note \"suboperation: coupling impact outline query deadcode vacuity graph complexity stubs vitality trace\")\n        (:target :type str :default \"\" :note \"target symbol package or file\")\n        (:symbol :type str :default \"\" :note \"symbol name\")\n        (:file :type str :default \"\" :note \"file path\")\n        (:strict :type bool :default false :note \"strict audit mode\")\n        (:filter :type str :default \"\" :note \"graph node filter\")\n        (:symbol :type str :note \"callers, status: the symbol\")\n        (:module :type str :note \"callers: restrict to one module (Python)\")\n        (:path :type str :note \"status: a file instead of a symbol\")\n        (:spec :type str :note \"coverage: the spec file\")\n        (:id :type str :note \"coverage: one requirement id\")\n        (:limit :type int :default 20 :note \"result limit\")\n        (:module :type str :default \"\" :note \"module path filter\")\n      )\n      :ops (:coupling :impact :outline :query :deadcode :vacuity :graph :complexity :stubs :vitality :trace)\n      :doc \"Unified Code Intelligence: whole-repo call graph, execution complexity metrics, stub detection, runtime hot-path tracing, package coupling DAG, blast radius impact, dead code detection, vacuity audit, and bounded outline extraction.\")\n\n    (:op :read\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Return a symbol or bounded slice of a file.\"\n      :form \"(:read :file <path> [:symbol <sym>] [:anchor <str>] [:limit <int>] [:start <int>] [:end <int>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :req true :note \"path to file in repository\")\n        (:symbol :type str :default \"\" :note \"symbol definition to extract\")\n        (:anchor :type str :default \"\" :note \"text anchor substring\")\n        (:limit :type int :default 200 :note \"maximum line count to return\")\n        (:start :type int :default 0 :note \"starting line number for slice\")\n        (:end :type int :default 0 :note \"ending line number for slice\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:read :file \\\"asl/grammar/rules.asn\\\" :limit 10)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND ERR_SYMBOL_NOT_FOUND ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION ERR_ANCHOR_NOT_FOUND ERR_BINARY)\n      :related (query)\n      :doc \"Bounded AST symbol and slice retrieval without whole-file dumping; a binary file (NUL in the first 8 KB or a known magic) is rejected with ERR_BINARY, :bytes and :kind, never returned.\")\n\n    (:op :query\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Search code for definitions and uses of a name; :in text searches comments, docs, memories and data instead, each labelled.\"\n      :form \"(:query :text <str> [:in code|text|all] [:limit <int>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:text :type str :req true :note \"substring or symbol query text\")\n        (:in :type sym :default :code :note \"code: definitions confirmed against the symbol index, then code lines where the text is code, and a :text count of what else matched; text: sections :comment (comments and strings in code) :doc :memory :data; all: both\")\n        (:limit :type int :default 20 :note \"maximum definition and hit count per section\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:query :text \\\"rules\\\" :limit 5)\"\n        \"(:query :text \\\"rules\\\" :in text)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_QUERY_FAILED)\n      :related (read observe)\n      :doc \"A mention outside code is not a use: it is counted under :text. Matching binary files are skipped, counted as :binarySkipped. Every call site of a function, through aliases and modules: (:observe :dim callers).\")\n\n    (:op :edit\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Stage a string replacement in the session buffer.\"\n      :form \"(:edit :file <path> :old <str> :new <str> [:all <bool>] [:autofix <sym>] [:force <bool>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :req true :note \"path to target file\")\n        (:old :type str :req true :note \"exact target string to replace\")\n        (:new :type str :req true :note \"replacement string\")\n        (:all :type bool :default false :note \"replace all occurrences\")\n        (:autofix :type sym :default :none :note \"structural or heuristic delimiter repair\")\n        (:force :type bool :default false :note \"stage despite balance or syntax errors\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:edit :file \\\"asl/grammar/rules.asn\\\" :old \\\"rules\\\" :new \\\"rules\\\" :all true)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND ERR_NO_MATCH ERR_AMBIGUOUS ERR_UNBALANCED)\n      :related (diff flush discard check txn)\n      :doc \"Atomic string replacement staged in the session buffer; rejected when the staged result breaks delimiter balance or syntax. :all replaces every occurrence, :autofix (true, indentation or heuristic) stages a delimiter repair, :force stages anyway.\")\n\n    (:op :write\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Stage whole-file content in the session buffer.\"\n      :form \"(:write :file <path> :content <str> [:force <bool>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :req true :note \"path to target file\")\n        (:content :type str :req true :note \"complete staged file content\")\n        (:force :type bool :default false :note \"stage despite balance or syntax errors\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:write :file \\\".asl/scratch.asn\\\" :content \\\"(:scratch true)\\\" :force true)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION ERR_IS_DIRECTORY ERR_UNBALANCED ERR_WRITE_FAILED)\n      :related (edit diff flush discard)\n      :doc \"Stage whole-file content in the session buffer, validated like edit; only flush touches disk.\")\n\n    (:op :tree\n      :scope toolchain\n      :form \"(:tree [:path <path>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:path :type str :default \".\" :note \"directory path to scan\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:tree :path \\\".\\\")\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_PATH_NOT_FOUND ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION)\n      :related (read query)\n      :doc \"Count files and directories under :path inside the workspace.\")\n\n    (:op :observe\n      :scope toolchain\n      :form \"(:observe :dim <tokenCost|memory|session|callers|status|coverage> [:scope p] [:limit n] [:symbol s] [:module m] [:path p] [:spec p] [:id r])\"\n      :params (\n        (:dim :type sym :req true :note \"callers: call sites of :symbol with path:line and kind, :possible, :excluded decoys; status: stub, callers, executing tests of :symbol or :path; coverage: :spec requirements implemented/tested; tokenCost: tokens by kind; memory: .asl/mem ledger sizes; session: agent sessions and :overlaps\")\n        (:scope :type str :default \".\" :note \"tokenCost: tracked files under this path\")\n        (:limit :type int :default 20 :note \"tokenCost :top or sessions shown, rest in :more; 1-100; receipt < 4096 bytes\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:observe :dim callers :symbol \\\"Cache.fetch\\\")\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_UNKNOWN_DIM ERR_NO_ENCODER ERR_BAD_ARG ERR_PATH_NOT_FOUND ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION ERR_EXEC_FAILED)\n      :doc \"Read-only workspace facts; an unknown :dim lists :nearest.\")\n\n    (:op :diff\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Show staged changes against disk.\"\n      :form \"(:diff [:file <path>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :default \"\" :note \"optional path to inspect; defaults to all staged\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:diff)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION)\n      :related (edit write flush discard)\n      :doc \"Show staged changes in the session buffer against disk.\")\n\n    (:op :flush\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Write all staged changes to disk atomically.\"\n      :form \"(:flush [:file <path>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :default \"\" :note \"optional path to persist; defaults to all staged\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:flush)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION ERR_NOT_STAGED ERR_SYNTAX_MALFORMATION ERR_STALE_BASE ERR_WRITE_FAILED)\n      :related (diff discard edit txn)\n      :doc \"Write all staged changes of the session buffer to disk atomically (fsync and rename); ERR_STALE_BASE when disk changed since staging.\")\n\n    (:op :discard\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Drop all staged changes.\"\n      :form \"(:discard [:file <path>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :default \"\" :note \"optional path to discard; defaults to all staged\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:discard)\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION)\n      :related (diff flush edit)\n      :doc \"Drop all staged changes of the session buffer without touching disk.\")\n\n    (:op :check\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Check a file: delimiter balance, then for an .asl file the stage-0 host check on staged content.\"\n      :form \"(:check [:file <path>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :default \"\" :note \"file to verify; defaults to workspace check\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:check :file \\\"asl/grammar/rules.asn\\\")\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION ERR_SYNTAX ERR_UNBALANCED_DELIMITERS ERR_CHECK_FAILED ERR_HOST_ABSENT ERR_WORKSPACE_CHECK_FAILED)\n      :related (test fix edit)\n      :doc \"Verify delimiter balance of an ASL or ASN file, or run a local syntax checker on a foreign one. A balanced .asl file then goes to asl/host/out/asl-host check on the content the next flush would write, which resolves imports and names and checks arity; its exit is :checkerExit and its diagnostics come back in :message. Without :file it runs asl check over the workspace: balance of every tracked ASL and ASN file and asl/host/out/asl-host check of each .asl.\")\n\n    (:op :test\n      :scope asl\n      :public \"Run an ASL test file on the stage-0 host against staged content.\"\n      :form \"(:test :file <path>)\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :req true :note \"path to ASL test file to execute\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:test :file \\\"asl/packages/asl-parser/tests/readerTest.asl\\\")\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_TEST_FAILED ERR_VACUOUS_PASS ERR_HOST_ABSENT ERR_EXEC_FAILED)\n      :related (check fix)\n      :doc \"Run asl/host/out/asl-host test on the file as the next flush would write it: an unknown name is an error, assert takes only true or false, and runTests must return true. It passes only with a positive executed :assertCount; a failure carries the host's :exit, the asserts run before it, and its diagnostics.\")\n\n    (:op :fix\n      :scope asl\n      :public \"Propose or stage minimal delimiter repair.\"\n      :form \"(:fix :file <path> [:apply <sym>])\"\n      :params (\n        (:file :type str :req true :note \"path to ASL or ASN file to balance\")\n        (:apply :type sym :default :none :note \"stage proposed repair (:true, :indentation, :heuristic)\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:fix :file \\\"asl/grammar/rules.asn\\\")\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_FILE_NOT_FOUND ERR_UNSUPPORTED_LANGUAGE ERR_AMBIGUOUS_REPAIR ERR_UNREPAIRABLE)\n      :related (check test edit)\n      :doc \"Propose, or with :apply stage, the minimal delimiter repair of an ASL/ASN file when it is structurally unique; an indentation tie-break is staged only with :apply :indentation.\")\n\n    (:op :txn\n      :scope any\n      :public \"Run nested edits and gates atomically inside owns.\"\n      :form \"(:txn :owns (<path> ...) <form> ...)\"\n      :params (\n        (:owns :type forms :req true :note \"path prefixes permitted to mutate\")\n      )\n      :examples (\n        \"(:txn :owns (\\\"asl/grammar\\\") (:check :file \\\"asl/grammar/rules.asn\\\"))\"\n      )\n      :errors (ERR_MISSING_ARG ERR_OWNS ERR_TXN_FORBIDDEN ERR_TXN_ABORTED ERR_TXN_FLUSH_FAILED)\n      :related (edit check flush discard)\n      :doc \"Stage nested edits inside :owns, run nested gates on staged content, flush only if all pass, else restore.\")\n\n    (:op :audit\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:subcmd :type sym :default :consistency :note \"subcommand to audit\")\n      )\n      :subcmds (:consistency :gates :coupling :closure :foreign :steps :deadcode :vacuity :sweep :graph :complexity :stubs :vitality :trace :all :full)\n      :doc \"Run systemic monorepo audit across declared dimensions including whole-repo sweep, dead code, test vacuity, stub detection, runtime tracing, and master system vitality.\")\n\n    (:op :crawl\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:url :type str :req true :note \"target URL to crawl\")\n        (:mode :type sym :default :auto :note \"crawler mode: auto staticHttp patchright\")\n        (:distill :type sym :default :asn :note \"distillation format: asn text raw\")\n      )\n      :doc \"Crawl target web page and distill DOM to pure Dyck-1 ASN without noise.\")\n\n    (:op :search\n      :scope toolchain\n      :brief \"(:search :query q [:limit n]) returns web results with a short answer\"\n      :params (\n        (:query :type str :req true :note \"search query string\")\n        (:limit :type int :default 3 :note \"maximum results to return\")\n      )\n      :doc \"Cognitive web search with provider cascading and direct fallback.\")\n\n    (:op :research\n      :scope toolchain\n      :brief \"(:research :topic t [:depth :flash|:deep|:exhaustive]) researches t on the web and returns a report whose facts carry their sources and a verification status\"\n      :params (\n        (:topic :type str :req true :note \"research topic inquiry\")\n        (:depth :type sym :default :flash :note \"one of :flash (3 results, gateway flash), :deep (5 results, gateway targeted), :exhaustive (5 results plus an adversarial search, gateway matrix); another value is rejected\")\n      )\n      :doc \"Web research through the gateway: the research route of its profile extracts facts; a report is :verified only when facts with source urls pass verification, else :unverified, :noEvidence or :failed with a :reason.\")\n\n    (:op :doctor\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params ()\n      :doc \"Audit measured capabilities and substrate invariants.\")\n\n    (:op :note\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:action :type sym :default :list :note \"action: list query write\")\n        (:kind :type sym :default :observation :note \"note category\")\n        (:scope :type sym :default :workspace :note \"scope tag\")\n        (:date :type str :default \"\" :note \"observation date\")\n        (:claim :type str :default \"\" :note \"claim or note content\")\n      )\n      :doc \"Record or query working memory observations in pure ASN.\")\n\n    (:op :target\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:name :type sym :default :list :note \"target generator name\")\n        (:file :type str :default \"\" :note \"target file path\")\n      )\n      :doc \"Compile ASL to standalone target code or synchronize distribution artifacts (sh, ps1, cmd, distrib, c, go, llvm, py, rs, swift, wat).\")\n\n    (:op :pack\n      :scope toolchain\n      :params (\n        (:target :type str :default \"all\" :note \"target platform architecture\")\n        (:quick :type bool :default false :note \"skip packaging archives\")\n        (:dist :type bool :default false :note \"build distribution bundles\")\n        (:install :type bool :default false :note \"install compiled binary\")\n        (:skipGates :type bool :default false :note \"skip verification gates\")\n        (:self :type bool :default false :note \"build host-only binary\")\n      )\n      :doc \"Assemble native self-hosted LLVM binary, audit verification gates, and package target distribution bundles (darwin-arm64, linux-x64, wasm).\")\n  ))\n")
(:file :tree "tc1" :path "asl/.asl.config.asn" :text "(:aslConfig\n  :workspace \"asl\"\n  :version \"0.1.0\"\n  :pureAsl true\n  :aslFirst true\n  :projections [\n    (:proj :from \"package.asn\" :to \"package.json\" :format \"json\" :doc \"Root ASL NPM manifest\")\n    (:proj :from \"web/package.asn\" :to \"web/package.json\" :format \"json\" :doc \"Web showcase package manifest\")\n    (:proj :from \"wrangler.asn\" :to \"wrangler.toml\" :format \"toml\" :doc \"Cloudflare Workers configuration\")\n  ]\n  :ignore [\n    \"scratch/**\"\n    \"tmp/**\"\n    \".asl/cache/**\"\n    \".asl/log/**\"\n    \"**/.system_generated/**\"\n    \"**/*.tmp\"\n    \"bench/*.lock\"\n    \"grammar/*.lock\"\n    \"prelude/*.lock\"\n    \".pre-commit-config.yaml\"\n    \"**/pnpm-lock.yaml\"\n    \"**/package-lock.json\"\n    \"**/pnpm-workspace.yaml\"\n    \"web/dist/**\"\n  ]\n  :gates [1 2 3 4 5 6 7]\n  :tokenBaseline 2\n  :telemetry (:targetTurnMs 100 :maxTokenCeiling 150)\n  :daemon (:resident true :memoryIndex true :maxFiles 2000)\n  :coverage (\n    :desired 75.0\n    :minAssertions 2\n    :strictPolarity false\n    :discountZeroAsserts true\n    :coreDesired 100.0\n    :corePackages [\"packages/asl-compiler\" \"packages/asl-parser\" \"packages/asl-codec\" \"packages/asl-lint\" \"packages/asl-gates\" \"packages/asl-pack\"]\n    :exclude [\"examples/**\" \"asl-arduino/**\" \"asl-quantum/**\"]\n  )\n  :tasks [\n    (:task :name \"project\" :cmd \"asl project\" :doc \"Transpile all declared ASN projections to host targets\")\n    (:task :name \"gate\" :cmd \"asl gate\" :doc \"Run full 7-gate pure ASL verification\")\n    (:task :name \"test\" :cmd \"asl test\" :doc \"Run native ASL test suites\")\n    (:task :name \"coverage\" :cmd \"asl coverage\" :doc \"Audit native function test coverage\")\n    (:task :name \"telemetry\" :cmd \"asl telemetry\" :doc \"Collect performance telemetry and token metrics\")\n    (:task :name \"web:transpile\" :cmd \"asl transpile-pkg web/package.asn web/package.json\" :doc \"Transpile web package.asn to package.json\")\n    (:task :name \"web:build\" :cmd \"asl task web:transpile && npm --prefix web run build\" :doc \"Build production web showcase\")\n    (:task :name \"web:dev\" :cmd \"asl task web:transpile && npm --prefix web run dev\" :doc \"Start Vite development server\")\n  ])\n")
(:file :tree "tc1" :path "asl/tools/observe/observe.asl" :text "(module ws/asl/tools/observe/observe\n  :x [runObserve main]\n  :i [(ws/asl/tools/observe/common :a c)\n      (ws/asl/tools/observe/args :a a)\n      (ws/asl/tools/observe/memory :a mem)\n      (ws/asl/tools/observe/session :a ses)\n      (ws/asl/tools/observe/callers :a cal)\n      (ws/asl/tools/observe/status :a sts)\n      (ws/asl/tools/observe/coverage :a cov)\n      (ws/asl/tools/observe/tokenCost :a tc)\n      (asl-regex/regex :a re)])\n\nfn dims -> (List String)\n  (list \"tokenCost\" \"memory\" \"session\" \"callers\" \"status\" \"coverage\")\n\nfn listDims? dim: String -> Bool\n  (or (= dim \"callers\") (= dim \"status\") (= dim \"coverage\"))\n\nfn finish r: (Result String String) -> c/Outcome\n  (mt r ((ok receipt) (c/Outcome :out (str receipt \"\\n\") :err \"\" :code 0)) ((err line) (c/rejected line)))\n\nfn crashOr r: (Result String String) -> c/Outcome\n  (mt r\n    ((ok receipt) (c/Outcome :out (str receipt \"\\n\") :err \"\" :code 0))\n    ((err line) (if (stringStartsWith? line \"(:observe \") (c/rejected line) (c/crashed line))))\n\nfn warned wr: (Pair String (Result String String)) -> c/Outcome\n  (let [(o (crashOr (pairSecond wr)))]\n    (c/Outcome :out o.out :err (str (pairFirst wr) o.err) :code o.code))\n\nfn parseLimit raw: String -> (Result Int64 String)\n  (mt (c/pyIntText (c/lstripChars raw \":\"))\n    ((none) (err (c/rejectLine \"ERR_BAD_ARG\" (str \":limit must be an integer, got \" raw) \"\")))\n    ((some n)\n      (let [(v (if (or (stringStartsWith? n \"-\") (> (stringLength n) 3)) (none) (stringToInt64 n)))]\n        (mt v\n          ((some k) (if (or (< k 1) (> k (c/limitMax))) (err (c/rejectLine \"ERR_BAD_ARG\" (str \":limit must be within 1..\" (stringFromInt64 (c/limitMax)) \", got \" n) \"\")) (ok k)))\n          ((none) (err (c/rejectLine \"ERR_BAD_ARG\" (str \":limit must be within 1..\" (stringFromInt64 (c/limitMax)) \", got \" n) \"\")))))))\n\nfn ! dispatch! ctx: c/Ctx args: a/Args dim: String limit: Int64 root: String scope: String -> c/Outcome\n  (let [(symbol (c/pyStrip args.symbol)) (pathArg (c/pyStrip args.path))]\n    (cond\n      ((= dim \"session\") (crashOr (ses/observeSession! root limit ctx)))\n      ((= dim \"memory\") (finish (mem/observeMemory! root ctx)))\n      ((= dim \"callers\")\n        (if (stringEmpty? symbol)\n          (c/rejected (c/rejectLine \"ERR_BAD_ARG\" \"callers needs :symbol <name>\" \"\"))\n          (warned (cal/observeCallers! root symbol (c/pyStrip args.module) limit ctx))))\n      ((= dim \"status\")\n        (if (= (not (stringEmpty? symbol)) (not (stringEmpty? pathArg)))\n          (c/rejected (c/rejectLine \"ERR_BAD_ARG\" \"status needs exactly one of :symbol <name> or :path <file>\" \"\"))\n          (mt (if (stringEmpty? pathArg) (ok \"\") (c/relPath! root pathArg \":path\"))\n            ((err line) (c/rejected line))\n            ((ok path) (warned (sts/observeStatus! root symbol path limit ctx))))))\n      ((= dim \"coverage\")\n        (if (stringEmpty? (c/pyStrip args.spec))\n          (c/rejected (c/rejectLine \"ERR_BAD_ARG\" \"coverage needs :spec <file>\" \"\"))\n          (mt (c/relPath! root (c/pyStrip args.spec) \":spec\")\n            ((err line) (c/rejected line))\n            ((ok spec)\n              (if (not (c/isFile? (c/joinPath root spec)))\n                (c/rejected (c/rejectLine \"ERR_BAD_ARG\" (str \":spec is not a file: \" args.spec) \"\"))\n                (if (stringEmpty? args.id)\n                  (warned (cov/observeCoverage! root spec (none) limit ctx))\n                  (mt (mt (unbalancedAt (stringToBytes args.id) 0 (bytesLength (stringToBytes args.id)) 0)\n                        ((some i) (err (str \"regex-compile: error at position \" (stringFromInt64 i) \": unmatched close parenthesis ')'\")))\n                        ((none) (re/regex-compile! args.id)))\n                    ((err e) (c/rejected (c/rejectLine \"ERR_BAD_ARG\" (str \":id is not a regular expression: \" (pyRegexError e)) \"\")))\n                    ((ok rx) (warned (cov/observeCoverage! root spec (some rx) limit ctx))))))))))\n      ((= dim \"tokenCost\") (finish (tc/observeTokenCost! root scope limit ctx)))\n      (else (c/rejected (c/rejectLine \"ERR_UNKNOWN_DIM\" (str \"unknown dimension \" dim) \"\")))))\n\nfn classEnd bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 first: Bool -> Int64\n  (cond\n    ((>= i n) n)\n    ((and first (= (bytesGet bs i) 94)) (classEnd bs (+ i 1) n true))\n    ((and first (= (bytesGet bs i) 93)) (classEnd bs (+ i 1) n false))\n    ((= (bytesGet bs i) 92) (classEnd bs (+ i 2) n false))\n    ((= (bytesGet bs i) 93) (+ i 1))\n    (else (classEnd bs (+ i 1) n false)))\n\nfn unbalancedAt bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 depth: Int64 -> (Option Int64)\n  (if (>= i n)\n    (none)\n    (let [(b (bytesGet bs i))]\n      (cond\n        ((= b 92) (unbalancedAt bs (+ i 2) n depth))\n        ((= b 91) (unbalancedAt bs (classEnd bs (+ i 1) n true) n depth))\n        ((= b 40) (unbalancedAt bs (+ i 1) n (+ depth 1)))\n        ((= b 41) (if (= depth 0) (some i) (unbalancedAt bs (+ i 1) n (- depth 1))))\n        (else (unbalancedAt bs (+ i 1) n depth)))))\n\nfn pyRegexError e: String -> String\n  (let [(rest (optionOr (stringSlice e (stringLength \"regex-compile: error at position \") (stringLength e)) e))\n        (colon (optionOr (stringIndexOf rest \": \") 0))\n        (pos (optionOr (stringSlice rest 0 colon) \"\"))\n        (what (optionOr (stringSlice rest (+ colon 2) (stringLength rest)) rest))]\n    (cond\n      ((stringStartsWith? what \"unclosed group\") (str \"missing ), unterminated subpattern at position \" pos))\n      ((stringStartsWith? what \"unclosed non-capturing group\") (str \"missing ), unterminated subpattern at position \" pos))\n      ((stringStartsWith? what \"unmatched close parenthesis\") (str \"unbalanced parenthesis at position \" pos))\n      ((stringStartsWith? what \"unclosed character class\") (str \"unterminated character set at position \" pos))\n      ((stringStartsWith? what \"trailing backslash\") (str \"bad escape (end of pattern) at position \" pos))\n      (else (str what \" at position \" pos))))\n\nfn ! runObserve ctx: c/Ctx argv: (List String) -> c/Outcome\n  (mt (a/parseArgs argv)\n    ((err o) o)\n    ((ok args)\n      (let [(dim (c/lstripChars (optionOr args.dim \"\") \":\"))]\n        (if (not (listContains? (dims) dim))\n          (c/rejected (c/rejectLine \"ERR_UNKNOWN_DIM\" (str \"unknown dimension \" dim \"; known: \" (c/joinWith (dims) \" \"))\n                                    (str \" :dim \" (c/quoted dim) \" :nearest (\" (c/joinWith (c/closeMatches dim (dims) 2 0.0) \" \") \")\")))\n          (let [(rawLimit (if (stringEmpty? (c/pyStrip args.limit)) (if (listDims? dim) \"100\" \"20\") args.limit))]\n            (mt (parseLimit rawLimit)\n              ((err line) (c/rejected line))\n              ((ok limit)\n                (mt (c/workspace! ctx)\n                  ((err line) (c/rejected line))\n                  ((ok root)\n                    (let [(scopeArg (c/pyStrip args.scope))]\n                      (mt (if (stringEmpty? scopeArg) (ok \"\") (c/relPath! root scopeArg \":scope\"))\n                        ((err line) (c/rejected line))\n                        ((ok scope) (dispatch! ctx args dim limit root scope)))))))))))))\n\nfn envPair row: String -> (Pair String String)\n  (mt (stringIndexOf row \"=\")\n    ((some i) (pair (optionOr (stringSlice row 0 i) row) (optionOr (stringSlice row (+ i 1) (stringLength row)) \"\")))\n    ((none) (pair row \"\")))\n\nfn ! main args: (List String) -> (Result Int64 String)\n  (mt (realPath \".\")\n    ((err e) (err e))\n    ((ok cwd)\n      (let [(ctx (c/Ctx :cwd cwd :env (map envPair (envList)) :spawnEnv (none) :now (/ (nowNs) 1000000000) :date \"\"))\n            (o (runObserve ctx args))]\n        (do\n          (if (stringEmpty? o.out) true (print o.out))\n          (if (stringEmpty? o.err) true (do (fdWrite 2 o.err) true))\n          (ok o.code)))))\n")
(:file :tree "tc1" :path "asl/tools/observe/args.asl" :text "(module ws/asl/tools/observe/args\n  :x [Args parseArgs usageText helpText]\n  :i [(ws/asl/tools/observe/common :a c)])\n\n(schema Args\n  (:f dim (Option String)) (:f scope String) (:f limit String) (:f symbol String) (:f module String)\n  (:f path String) (:f spec String) (:f id String))\n\nfn usageText -> String\n  (str \"usage: observe.asl [-h] --dim DIM [--scope SCOPE] [--limit LIMIT]\\n\"\n       \"                   [--symbol SYMBOL] [--module MODULE] [--path PATH]\\n\"\n       \"                   [--spec SPEC] [--id ID]\\n\")\n\nfn helpText -> String\n  (str (usageText) \"\\noptions:\\n  -h, --help       show this help message and exit\\n  --dim DIM\\n  --scope SCOPE\\n  --limit LIMIT\\n\"\n       \"  --symbol SYMBOL\\n  --module MODULE\\n  --path PATH\\n  --spec SPEC\\n  --id ID\\n\")\n\nfn optionStrings -> (List String)\n  (list \"-h\" \"--help\" \"--dim\" \"--scope\" \"--limit\" \"--symbol\" \"--module\" \"--path\" \"--spec\" \"--id\")\n\nfn actionOf opt: String -> String\n  (cond ((or (= opt \"-h\") (= opt \"--help\")) \"help\") (else (optionOr (stringSlice opt 2 (stringLength opt)) \"\")))\n\nfn actionName act: String -> String\n  (if (= act \"help\") \"-h/--help\" (str \"--\" act))\n\n(schema Opt (:f act (Option String)) (:f spelling String) (:f sep (Option String)) (:f explicit (Option String)))\n\n(enum Tok (:c tokArg [(s String)]) (:c tokSep [(s String)]) (:c tokOpt [(o Opt) (s String)]))\n\nfn usageError msg: String -> c/Outcome\n  (c/Outcome :out \"\" :err (str (usageText) \"observe.asl: error: \" msg \"\\n\") :code 2)\n\nfn partitionEq s: String -> (Pair String (Option String))\n  (mt (stringIndexOf s \"=\")\n    ((none) (pair s (none)))\n    ((some i) (pair (optionOr (stringSlice s 0 i) \"\") (some (optionOr (stringSlice s (+ i 1) (stringLength s)) \"\")))))\n\nfn negNumber? s: String -> Bool\n  (let [(body (optionOr (stringSlice s 1 (stringLength s)) \"\"))\n        (digits? (fn [(t String)] -> Bool (listAll? (fn [(ch String)] -> Bool (and (>= (charCode ch) 48) (<= (charCode ch) 57))) (stringChars t))))]\n    (and (stringStartsWith? s \"-\")\n         (or (and (not (stringEmpty? body)) (digits? body))\n             (mt (stringIndexOf body \".\")\n               ((none) false)\n               ((some i) (let [(a (optionOr (stringSlice body 0 i) \"\")) (b (optionOr (stringSlice body (+ i 1) (stringLength body)) \"\"))]\n                           (and (digits? a) (not (stringEmpty? b)) (digits? b))))))))\n\nfn optionTuples s: String -> (List Opt)\n  (if (stringStartsWith? s \"--\")\n    (let [(pe (partitionEq s))]\n      (map (fn [(o String)] -> Opt (Opt :act (some (actionOf o)) :spelling o :sep (optionMap (fn [(x String)] -> String \"=\") (pairSecond pe)) :explicit (pairSecond pe)))\n           (filter (fn [(o String)] -> Bool (stringStartsWith? o (pairFirst pe))) (optionStrings))))\n    (let [(short (optionOr (stringSlice s 0 2) s)) (rest (optionOr (stringSlice s 2 (stringLength s)) \"\"))]\n      (fold (fn [(acc (List Opt)) (o String)] -> (List Opt)\n              (cond ((= o short) (listAppend acc (list (Opt :act (some (actionOf o)) :spelling o :sep (some \"\") :explicit (some rest)))))\n                    ((stringStartsWith? o s) (listAppend acc (list (Opt :act (some (actionOf o)) :spelling o :sep (none) :explicit (none)))))\n                    (else acc)))\n            (list) (optionStrings))))\n\nfn classify s: String -> (Result Tok c/Outcome)\n  (cond\n    ((or (stringEmpty? s) (not (stringStartsWith? s \"-\"))) (ok (tokArg s)))\n    ((listContains? (optionStrings) s) (ok (tokOpt (Opt :act (some (actionOf s)) :spelling s :sep (none) :explicit (none)) s)))\n    ((= (stringLength s) 1) (ok (tokArg s)))\n    (else\n      (let [(pe (partitionEq s))]\n        (if (and (some? (pairSecond pe)) (listContains? (optionStrings) (pairFirst pe)))\n          (ok (tokOpt (Opt :act (some (actionOf (pairFirst pe))) :spelling (pairFirst pe) :sep (some \"=\") :explicit (pairSecond pe)) s))\n          (let [(tups (optionTuples s))]\n            (cond\n              ((> (listLength tups) 1)\n                (err (usageError (str \"ambiguous option: \" s \" could match \" (stringJoin (map (fn [(o Opt)] -> String o.spelling) tups) \", \")))))\n              ((= (listLength tups) 1) (ok (tokOpt (optionOr (listHead tups) (Opt :act (none) :spelling s :sep (none) :explicit (none))) s)))\n              ((negNumber? s) (ok (tokArg s)))\n              ((stringContains? s \" \") (ok (tokArg s)))\n              (else (ok (tokOpt (Opt :act (none) :spelling s :sep (none) :explicit (none)) s)))))))))\n\nfn classifyAll args: (List String) acc: (List Tok) -> (Result (List Tok) c/Outcome)\n  (mt (listHead args)\n    ((none) (ok (listReverse acc)))\n    ((some a)\n      (if (= a \"--\")\n        (ok (listAppend (listReverse acc) (cons (tokSep a) (map (fn [(x String)] -> Tok (tokArg x)) (optionOr (listTail args) (list))))))\n        (mt (classify a)\n          ((err o) (err o))\n          ((ok t) (classifyAll (optionOr (listTail args) (list)) (cons t acc)))))))\n\nfn pyRepr s: String -> String\n  (let [(q (if (and (stringContains? s \"'\") (not (stringContains? s \"\\\"\"))) \"\\\"\" \"'\"))\n        (body (stringJoin (map (fn [(ch String)] -> String\n                                 (let [(k (charCode ch))]\n                                   (cond ((= ch \"\\\\\") \"\\\\\\\\\") ((= ch q) (str \"\\\\\" q)) ((= ch \"\\n\") \"\\\\n\") ((= ch \"\\r\") \"\\\\r\") ((= ch \"\\t\") \"\\\\t\")\n                                         ((or (< k 32) (= k 127)) (str \"\\\\x\" (hex2 k))) (else ch))))\n                               (stringChars s)) \"\"))]\n    (str q body q))\n\nfn hexDigit n: Int64 -> String\n  (optionOr (stringSlice \"0123456789abcdef\" n (+ n 1)) \"0\")\n\nfn hex2 n: Int64 -> String\n  (str (hexDigit (/ n 16)) (hexDigit (mod n 16)))\n\n(schema St (:f args Args) (:f extras (List String)) (:f seen (List String)))\n\nfn setArg a: Args act: String v: String -> Args\n  (cond\n    ((= act \"dim\") (with a :dim (some v)))\n    ((= act \"scope\") (with a :scope v))\n    ((= act \"limit\") (with a :limit v))\n    ((= act \"symbol\") (with a :symbol v))\n    ((= act \"module\") (with a :module v))\n    ((= act \"path\") (with a :path v))\n    ((= act \"spec\") (with a :spec v))\n    (else (with a :id v)))\n\nfn helpOutcome -> c/Outcome\n  (c/Outcome :out (helpText) :err \"\" :code 0)\n\nfn shortTail st: St o: Opt -> (Result St c/Outcome)\n  (let [(ex (optionOr o.explicit \"\")) (sp (optionOr o.sep \"\"))]\n    (if (or (not (stringEmpty? sp)) (stringStartsWith? ex \"-\"))\n      (err (usageError (str \"argument -h/--help: ignored explicit argument \" (pyRepr ex))))\n      (err (helpOutcome))))\n\nfn tokAt toks: (List Tok) i: Int64 -> (Option Tok)\n  (listGet toks i)\n\nfn consumeOpt st: St o: Opt raw: String toks: (List Tok) i: Int64 -> (Result (Pair St Int64) c/Outcome)\n  (mt o.act\n    ((none) (ok (pair (with st :extras (listAppend st.extras (list raw))) (+ i 1))))\n    ((some act)\n      (mt o.explicit\n        ((some ex)\n          (cond\n            ((and (= act \"help\") (not (stringStartsWith? o.spelling \"--\")) (not (stringEmpty? ex)))\n              (mt (shortTail st o) ((ok s2) (ok (pair s2 (+ i 1)))) ((err e) (err e))))\n            ((= act \"help\") (err (usageError (str \"argument -h/--help: ignored explicit argument \" (pyRepr ex)))))\n            (else (ok (pair (with st :args (setArg st.args act ex) :seen (cons act st.seen)) (+ i 1))))))\n        ((none)\n          (if (= act \"help\")\n            (err (helpOutcome))\n            (mt (tokAt toks (+ i 1))\n              ((some nt) (mt nt\n                           ((tokArg v) (ok (pair (with st :args (setArg st.args act v) :seen (cons act st.seen)) (+ i 2))))\n                           (_ (err (usageError (str \"argument \" (actionName act) \": expected one argument\"))))))\n              ((none) (err (usageError (str \"argument \" (actionName act) \": expected one argument\"))))))))))\n\nfn walk st: St toks: (List Tok) i: Int64 -> (Result St c/Outcome)\n  (mt (tokAt toks i)\n    ((none) (ok st))\n    ((some t)\n      (mt t\n        ((tokOpt o raw) (mt (consumeOpt st o raw toks i) ((ok p) (walk (pairFirst p) toks (pairSecond p))) ((err e) (err e))))\n        ((tokArg s) (walk (with st :extras (listAppend st.extras (list s))) toks (+ i 1)))\n        ((tokSep s) (walk (with st :extras (listAppend st.extras (list s))) toks (+ i 1))))))\n\nfn parseArgs argv: (List String) -> (Result Args c/Outcome)\n  (mt (classifyAll argv (list))\n    ((err e) (err e))\n    ((ok toks)\n      (mt (walk (St :args (Args :dim (none) :scope \"\" :limit \"\" :symbol \"\" :module \"\" :path \"\" :spec \"\" :id \"\") :extras (list) :seen (list)) toks 0)\n        ((err e) (err e))\n        ((ok st)\n          (cond\n            ((not (listContains? st.seen \"dim\")) (err (usageError \"the following arguments are required: --dim\")))\n            ((not (listEmpty? st.extras)) (err (usageError (str \"unrecognized arguments: \" (stringJoin st.extras \" \")))))\n            (else (ok st.args)))))))\n")
(:file :tree "tc1" :path "asl/tools/observe/common.asl" :text "(module ws/asl/tools/observe/common\n  :x [Ctx Outcome Proc Section\n      ctxEnv ctxHome esc rejectLine rejected crashed receiptMax limitMax\n      runArgv! git! workspace! shortRev! workspaceFiles!\n      joinPath dirName baseName splitExt isAbs lexists? isDir? isFile? isLink? realPathLoose! relPath!\n      pyIntText lstripChars rstripChars stripChars pyStrip pyIsSpaceCode\n      fitReceipt atStr quoted sortUnique dedupe byteLen lines keepEndsLines\n      closeMatches charCodes utf8Replace mapGetOr utf8Valid? spaceLenAt findFrom universalNewlines catAll joinWith splitByte]\n  :i [(asl-forms/similarity :a sim)])\n\n(schema Ctx\n  (:f cwd String)\n  (:f env (List (Pair String String)))\n  (:f spawnEnv (Option (List String)))\n  (:f now Int64)\n  (:f date String))\n\n(schema Outcome (:f out String) (:f err String) (:f code Int64))\n\n(schema Proc (:f code Int64) (:f out String) (:f errText String))\n\n(schema Section (:f key String) (:f items (List String)) (:f limit Int64))\n\nfn receiptMax -> Int64\n  4096\n\nfn limitMax -> Int64\n  100\n\nfn mapGetOr kv: (List (Pair String String)) k: String -> (Option String)\n  (mt (listHead kv)\n    ((none) (none))\n    ((some p) (if (= (pairFirst p) k) (some (pairSecond p)) (mapGetOr (optionOr (listTail kv) (list)) k))))\n\nfn ctxEnv ctx: Ctx k: String -> (Option String)\n  (mapGetOr ctx.env k)\n\nfn ctxHome ctx: Ctx -> String\n  (optionOr (ctxEnv ctx \"HOME\") \"\")\n\nfn esc s: String -> String\n  (stringReplace (stringReplace (stringReplace s \"\\\\\" \"\\\\\\\\\") \"\\\"\" \"\\\\\\\"\") \"\\n\" \"\\\\n\")\n\nfn rejectLine code: String message: String extra: String -> String\n  (str \"(:observe :status :rejected :error \" code extra \" :message \\\"\" (esc message) \"\\\")\")\n\nfn rejected line: String -> Outcome\n  (Outcome :out (str line \"\\n\") :err \"\" :code 1)\n\nfn crashed message: String -> Outcome\n  (Outcome :out \"\" :err (str message \"\\n\") :code 1)\n\nfn quoted s: String -> String\n  (str \"\\\"\" (esc s) \"\\\"\")\n\nfn atStr rel: String line: Int64 -> String\n  (str \"\\\"\" (esc rel) \":\" (stringFromInt64 line) \"\\\"\")\n\nfn byteLen s: String -> Int64\n  (stringLength s)\n\n(schema Pump (:f outOpen Bool) (:f errOpen Bool) (:f out (List String)) (:f errs (List String)))\n\nfn ! readSide fd: Int64 -> (Pair Bool String)\n  (mt (fdRead fd 65536)\n    ((ok chunk) (if (stringEmpty? chunk) (do (fdClose fd) (pair false \"\")) (pair true chunk)))\n    ((err e) (if (= e \"wouldBlock\") (pair true \"\") (do (fdClose fd) (pair false \"\")))))\n\nfn ! pump sp: SpawnedProc st: Pump -> Pump\n  (if (not (or st.outOpen st.errOpen))\n    st\n    (let [(fds (listAppend (if st.outOpen (list (pair sp.stdout 1)) (list)) (if st.errOpen (list (pair sp.stderr 1)) (list))))]\n      (mt (fdPoll fds 60000)\n        ((err e) (if (= e \"interrupted\") (pump sp st) (with st :outOpen false :errOpen false :errs (cons (str \"poll: \" e) st.errs))))\n        ((ok ready)\n          (let [(ro (and st.outOpen (listAny? (fn [(p (Pair Int64 Int64))] -> Bool (= (pairFirst p) sp.stdout)) ready)))\n                (re (and st.errOpen (listAny? (fn [(p (Pair Int64 Int64))] -> Bool (= (pairFirst p) sp.stderr)) ready)))\n                (o (if ro (readSide sp.stdout) (pair st.outOpen \"\")))\n                (e2 (if re (readSide sp.stderr) (pair st.errOpen \"\")))]\n            (pump sp (Pump :outOpen (pairFirst o) :errOpen (pairFirst e2)\n                           :out (if (stringEmpty? (pairSecond o)) st.out (cons (pairSecond o) st.out))\n                           :errs (if (stringEmpty? (pairSecond e2)) st.errs (cons (pairSecond e2) st.errs)))))))))\n\nfn ! runArgv! argv: (List String) cwd: String ctx: Ctx -> (Result Proc String)\n  (mt (procSpawnv argv (some cwd) ctx.spawnEnv)\n    ((err e) (err e))\n    ((ok sp)\n      (do\n        (fdClose sp.stdin)\n        (let [(st (pump sp (Pump :outOpen true :errOpen true :out (list) :errs (list))))]\n          (mt (procWaitPid sp.pid false)\n            ((err e) (err e))\n            ((ok code) (ok (Proc :code (optionOr code -1) :out (catAll (listReverse st.out)) :errText (catAll (listReverse st.errs))))))))))\n\nfn ! git! args: (List String) root: String ctx: Ctx -> (Result (Pair Int64 String) String)\n  (mt (runArgv! (cons \"git\" args) root ctx)\n    ((ok p) (ok (pair p.code p.out)))\n    ((err e) (err (rejectLine \"ERR_TOOL_ABSENT\" (str \"git could not be run (\" e \"); observe reads the workspace through git\") \"\"))))\n\nfn ! workspace! ctx: Ctx -> (Result String String)\n  (mt (git! (list \"rev-parse\" \"--show-toplevel\") ctx.cwd ctx)\n    ((err e) (err e))\n    ((ok p) (let [(top (pyStrip (pairSecond p)))] (ok (if (and (= (pairFirst p) 0) (not (stringEmpty? top))) top ctx.cwd)))))\n\nfn ! shortRev! root: String ctx: Ctx -> (Result String String)\n  (mt (git! (list \"rev-parse\" \"--short\" \"HEAD\") root ctx)\n    ((err e) (err e))\n    ((ok p) (let [(r (pyStrip (pairSecond p)))] (ok (if (and (= (pairFirst p) 0) (not (stringEmpty? r))) r \"none\")))))\n\nfn ! workspaceFiles! root: String ctx: Ctx -> (Result (List String) String)\n  (mt (git! (list \"ls-files\" \"-z\" \"-co\" \"--exclude-standard\") root ctx)\n    ((err e) (err e))\n    ((ok p)\n      (if (!= (pairFirst p) 0)\n        (err (rejectLine \"ERR_GIT\" (str \"git ls-files failed in \" root) \"\"))\n        (ok (filter (fn [(rel String)] -> Bool (isFile? (joinPath root rel)))\n                    (sortUnique (filter (fn [(x String)] -> Bool (not (stringEmpty? x))) (splitByte (pairSecond p) 0))))))))\n\nfn isAbs p: String -> Bool\n  (stringStartsWith? p \"/\")\n\nfn joinPath a: String b: String -> String\n  (cond ((isAbs b) b) ((stringEmpty? a) b) ((stringEndsWith? a \"/\") (str a b)) (else (str a \"/\" b)))\n\nfn lastSlash s: String i: Int64 -> Int64\n  (cond ((< i 0) -1) ((= (optionOr (stringSlice s i (+ i 1)) \"\") \"/\") i) (else (lastSlash s (- i 1))))\n\nfn dirName p: String -> String\n  (let [(i (lastSlash p (- (stringLength p) 1)))]\n    (if (< i 0) \"\" (let [(head (optionOr (stringSlice p 0 (+ i 1)) \"\"))] (let [(t (rstripChars head \"/\"))] (if (stringEmpty? t) head t)))))\n\nfn baseName p: String -> String\n  (let [(i (lastSlash p (- (stringLength p) 1)))]\n    (optionOr (stringSlice p (+ i 1) (stringLength p)) p))\n\nfn lastDot s: String i: Int64 -> Int64\n  (cond ((< i 0) -1) ((= (optionOr (stringSlice s i (+ i 1)) \"\") \".\") i) (else (lastDot s (- i 1))))\n\nfn allDots? s: String i: Int64 -> Bool\n  (cond ((< i 0) true) ((= (optionOr (stringSlice s i (+ i 1)) \"\") \".\") (allDots? s (- i 1))) (else false))\n\nfn splitExt p: String -> (Pair String String)\n  (let [(b (baseName p)) (i (lastDot b (- (stringLength b) 1)))]\n    (if (or (< i 0) (allDots? b (- i 1)))\n      (pair p \"\")\n      (let [(cut (- (stringLength p) (- (stringLength b) i)))]\n        (pair (optionOr (stringSlice p 0 cut) p) (optionOr (stringSlice p cut (stringLength p)) \"\")))))\n\nfn ! lexists? p: String -> Bool\n  (ok? (fileStat p))\n\nfn ! isDir? p: String -> Bool\n  (mt (fileStat p) ((ok s) s.isDir) ((err _) false))\n\nfn ! isFile? p: String -> Bool\n  (mt (fileStat p) ((ok s) s.isFile) ((err _) false))\n\nfn ! isLink? p: String -> Bool\n  (let [(parent (dirName p)) (name (baseName p))]\n    (mt (realPath p)\n      ((err _) false)\n      ((ok r) (mt (realPath (if (stringEmpty? parent) \".\" parent))\n                ((ok pr) (!= r (joinPath pr name)))\n                ((err _) false)))))\n\nfn loosePart! cur: String parts: (List String) -> String\n  (mt (listHead parts)\n    ((none) (if (stringEmpty? cur) \"/\" cur))\n    ((some c)\n      (let [(rest (optionOr (listTail parts) (list)))]\n        (cond\n          ((or (stringEmpty? c) (= c \".\")) (loosePart! cur rest))\n          ((= c \"..\") (loosePart! (let [(d (dirName cur))] (if (= d \"/\") \"\" d)) rest))\n          (else (let [(nxt (str cur \"/\" c))]\n                  (mt (realPath nxt)\n                    ((ok r) (loosePart! (if (= r \"/\") \"\" r) rest))\n                    ((err _) (loosePart! nxt rest)))))))))\n\nfn realPathLoose! p: String cwd: String -> String\n  (let [(full (if (isAbs p) p (joinPath cwd p)))]\n    (loosePart! \"\" (stringSplit full \"/\")))\n\nfn relPath! root: String arg: String what: String -> (Result String String)\n  (let [(full (realPathLoose! (joinPath root arg) root))\n        (base (realPathLoose! root root))]\n    (cond\n      ((and (!= full base) (not (stringStartsWith? full (str base \"/\"))))\n        (err (rejectLine \"ERR_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION\" (str what \" resolves outside the workspace: \" arg) \"\")))\n      ((not (lexists? full))\n        (err (rejectLine \"ERR_PATH_NOT_FOUND\" (str what \" not found: \" arg) \"\")))\n      ((= full base) (ok \"\"))\n      (else (ok (optionOr (stringSlice full (+ (stringLength base) 1) (stringLength full)) \"\")))))\n\nfn charAt s: String i: Int64 -> String\n  (optionOr (stringSlice s i (+ i 1)) \"\")\n\nfn inChars? c: String chars: String -> Bool\n  (and (not (stringEmpty? c)) (stringContains? chars c))\n\nfn lstripFrom s: String chars: String i: Int64 -> Int64\n  (if (and (< i (stringLength s)) (inChars? (charAt s i) chars)) (lstripFrom s chars (+ i 1)) i)\n\nfn rstripFrom s: String chars: String i: Int64 -> Int64\n  (if (and (> i 0) (inChars? (charAt s (- i 1)) chars)) (rstripFrom s chars (- i 1)) i)\n\nfn lstripChars s: String chars: String -> String\n  (optionOr (stringSlice s (lstripFrom s chars 0) (stringLength s)) \"\")\n\nfn rstripChars s: String chars: String -> String\n  (optionOr (stringSlice s 0 (rstripFrom s chars (stringLength s))) \"\")\n\nfn stripChars s: String chars: String -> String\n  (lstripChars (rstripChars s chars) chars)\n\nfn pyIsSpaceCode c: Int64 -> Bool\n  (or (and (>= c 9) (<= c 13)) (and (>= c 28) (<= c 32)) (= c 133) (= c 160) (= c 5760) (and (>= c 8192) (<= c 8202))\n      (= c 8232) (= c 8233) (= c 8239) (= c 8287) (= c 12288))\n\nfn contAt? bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 -> Bool\n  (and (< i n) (>= (bytesGet bs i) 128) (<= (bytesGet bs i) 191))\n\nfn codeAt bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 -> (Pair Int64 Int64)\n  (let [(b0 (bytesGet bs i))\n        (need (cond ((< b0 128) 1) ((and (>= b0 194) (< b0 224)) 2) ((and (>= b0 224) (< b0 240)) 3) ((and (>= b0 240) (< b0 245)) 4) (else 0)))]\n    (cond\n      ((= need 0) (pair -1 1))\n      ((= need 1) (pair b0 1))\n      (else\n        (let [(lo1 (cond ((= b0 224) 160) ((= b0 240) 144) (else 128)))\n              (hi1 (cond ((= b0 237) 159) ((= b0 244) 143) (else 191)))\n              (b1 (if (< (+ i 1) n) (bytesGet bs (+ i 1)) -1))]\n          (cond\n            ((or (< b1 lo1) (> b1 hi1)) (pair -1 1))\n            ((= need 2) (pair (+ (* (- b0 192) 64) (- b1 128)) 2))\n            ((not (contAt? bs (+ i 2) n)) (pair -1 2))\n            ((= need 3) (pair (+ (* (- b0 224) 4096) (* (- b1 128) 64) (- (bytesGet bs (+ i 2)) 128)) 3))\n            ((not (contAt? bs (+ i 3) n)) (pair -1 3))\n            (else (pair (+ (* (- b0 240) 262144) (* (- b1 128) 4096) (* (- (bytesGet bs (+ i 2)) 128) 64) (- (bytesGet bs (+ i 3)) 128)) 4)))))))\n\nfn validLoop bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 -> Bool\n  (cond\n    ((>= i n) true)\n    ((< (bytesGet bs i) 128) (validLoop bs (+ i 1) n))\n    (else (let [(c (codeAt bs i n))] (if (< (pairFirst c) 0) false (validLoop bs (+ i (pairSecond c)) n)))))\n\nfn utf8Valid? s: String -> Bool\n  (let [(bs (stringToBytes s))] (validLoop bs 0 (bytesLength bs)))\n\nfn spaceLenAt bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 -> Int64\n  (if (>= i n)\n    0\n    (let [(b (bytesGet bs i))]\n      (if (< b 128)\n        (if (pyIsSpaceCode b) 1 0)\n        (let [(c (codeAt bs i n))] (if (and (>= (pairFirst c) 0) (pyIsSpaceCode (pairFirst c))) (pairSecond c) 0)))))\n\nfn matchAt bs: Bytes pat: Bytes i: Int64 k: Int64 m: Int64 -> Bool\n  (cond ((>= k m) true) ((= (bytesGet bs (+ i k)) (bytesGet pat k)) (matchAt bs pat i (+ k 1) m)) (else false))\n\nfn findFrom bs: Bytes n: Int64 pat: Bytes i: Int64 -> Int64\n  (let [(m (bytesLength pat))]\n    (cond ((> (+ i m) n) -1) ((matchAt bs pat i 0 m) i) (else (findFrom bs n pat (+ i 1)))))\n\nfn codesLoop bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 acc: (List (Pair Int64 Int64)) -> (List (Pair Int64 Int64))\n  (if (>= i n)\n    (listReverse acc)\n    (let [(c (codeAt bs i n))]\n      (codesLoop bs (+ i (pairSecond c)) n (cons (pair (pairFirst c) i) acc))))\n\nfn charCodes s: String -> (List (Pair Int64 Int64))\n  (let [(bs (stringToBytes s))] (codesLoop bs 0 (bytesLength bs) (list)))\n\nfn replaceLoop s: String bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 start: Int64 acc: (List String) -> (List String)\n  (if (>= i n)\n    (listReverse (cons (optionOr (stringSlice s start n) \"\") acc))\n    (let [(c (codeAt bs i n))]\n      (if (< (pairFirst c) 0)\n        (replaceLoop s bs (+ i (pairSecond c)) n (+ i (pairSecond c)) (cons \"\\xef\\xbf\\xbd\" (cons (optionOr (stringSlice s start i) \"\") acc)))\n        (replaceLoop s bs (+ i (pairSecond c)) n start acc))))\n\nfn utf8Replace s: String -> String\n  (let [(bs (stringToBytes s))] (catAll (replaceLoop s bs 0 (bytesLength bs) 0 (list))))\n\nfn pyStripStart codes: (List (Pair Int64 Int64)) -> (List (Pair Int64 Int64))\n  (mt (listHead codes)\n    ((none) codes)\n    ((some c) (if (pyIsSpaceCode (pairFirst c)) (pyStripStart (optionOr (listTail codes) (list))) codes)))\n\nfn pyStrip s: String -> String\n  (let [(codes (pyStripStart (charCodes s)))]\n    (mt (listHead codes)\n      ((none) \"\")\n      ((some first)\n        (let [(back (pyStripStart (listReverse codes)))]\n          (mt (listHead back)\n            ((none) \"\")\n            ((some last) (let [(endAt (+ (pairSecond last) (pairSecond (codeAt (stringToBytes s) (pairSecond last) (stringLength s)))))]\n                           (optionOr (stringSlice s (pairSecond first) endAt) \"\"))))))))\n\nfn digit? c: String -> Bool\n  (and (= (stringLength c) 1) (>= (charCode c) 48) (<= (charCode c) 57))\n\nfn digitsOk? s: String i: Int64 prevDigit: Bool -> Bool\n  (if (>= i (stringLength s))\n    prevDigit\n    (let [(c (charAt s i))]\n      (cond ((digit? c) (digitsOk? s (+ i 1) true))\n            ((and (= c \"_\") prevDigit) (digitsOk? s (+ i 1) false))\n            (else false))))\n\nfn pyIntText raw: String -> (Option String)\n  (let [(s (pyStrip raw))\n        (neg (stringStartsWith? s \"-\"))\n        (body (if (or neg (stringStartsWith? s \"+\")) (optionOr (stringSlice s 1 (stringLength s)) \"\") s))]\n    (if (or (stringEmpty? body) (not (digit? (charAt body 0))) (not (digitsOk? body 0 false)))\n      (none)\n      (let [(digits (lstripChars (stringReplace body \"_\" \"\") \"0\"))\n            (mag (if (stringEmpty? digits) \"0\" digits))]\n        (some (if (and neg (!= mag \"0\")) (str \"-\" mag) mag)))))\n\nfn sortUnique xs: (List String) -> (List String)\n  (dedupe (listSort xs) (list))\n\nfn dedupe xs: (List String) acc: (List String) -> (List String)\n  (mt (listHead xs)\n    ((none) (listReverse acc))\n    ((some x) (dedupe (optionOr (listTail xs) (list)) (if (= (optionOr (listHead acc) \"\\x00none\") x) acc (cons x acc)))))\n\nfn linesLoop s: String i: Int64 start: Int64 n: Int64 acc: (List String) -> (List String)\n  (cond\n    ((>= i n) (listReverse (if (< start n) (cons (optionOr (stringSlice s start n) \"\") acc) acc)))\n    ((= (charAt s i) \"\\n\") (linesLoop s (+ i 1) (+ i 1) n (cons (optionOr (stringSlice s start (+ i 1)) \"\") acc)))\n    (else (linesLoop s (+ i 1) start n acc)))\n\nfn keepEndsLines s: String -> (List String)\n  (let [(bs (stringToBytes s))] (keepEndsBytes s bs 0 0 (bytesLength bs) (list)))\n\nfn keepEndsBytes s: String bs: Bytes i: Int64 start: Int64 n: Int64 acc: (List String) -> (List String)\n  (cond\n    ((>= i n) (listReverse (if (< start n) (cons (optionOr (stringSlice s start n) \"\") acc) acc)))\n    ((= (bytesGet bs i) 10) (keepEndsBytes s bs (+ i 1) (+ i 1) n (cons (optionOr (stringSlice s start (+ i 1)) \"\") acc)))\n    (else (keepEndsBytes s bs (+ i 1) start n acc)))\n\nfn catAll xs: (List String) -> String\n  (let [(n (listLength xs))]\n    (cond ((= n 0) \"\") ((= n 1) (optionOr (listHead xs) \"\")) ((= n 2) (stringConcat (optionOr (listHead xs) \"\") (optionOr (listGet xs 1) \"\")))\n          (else (let [(h (/ n 2))] (stringConcat (catAll (listTake xs h)) (catAll (listDrop xs h)))))))\n\nfn interleave xs: (List String) sep: String acc: (List String) -> (List String)\n  (mt (listHead xs)\n    ((none) (listReverse acc))\n    ((some x) (interleave (optionOr (listTail xs) (list)) sep (cons x (if (listEmpty? acc) acc (cons sep acc))))))\n\nfn joinWith xs: (List String) sep: String -> String\n  (catAll (interleave xs sep (list)))\n\nfn splitLoop s: String bs: Bytes b: Int64 i: Int64 start: Int64 n: Int64 acc: (List String) -> (List String)\n  (cond\n    ((>= i n) (listReverse (cons (optionOr (stringSlice s start n) \"\") acc)))\n    ((= (bytesGet bs i) b) (splitLoop s bs b (+ i 1) (+ i 1) n (cons (optionOr (stringSlice s start i) \"\") acc)))\n    (else (splitLoop s bs b (+ i 1) start n acc)))\n\nfn splitByte s: String b: Int64 -> (List String)\n  (let [(bs (stringToBytes s))] (splitLoop s bs b 0 0 (bytesLength bs) (list)))\n\nfn crLoop s: String bs: Bytes i: Int64 start: Int64 n: Int64 acc: (List String) -> (List String)\n  (cond\n    ((>= i n) (listReverse (cons (optionOr (stringSlice s start n) \"\") acc)))\n    ((= (bytesGet bs i) 13)\n      (let [(skip (if (and (< (+ i 1) n) (= (bytesGet bs (+ i 1)) 10)) 2 1))]\n        (crLoop s bs (+ i skip) (+ i skip) n (cons \"\\n\" (cons (optionOr (stringSlice s start i) \"\") acc)))))\n    (else (crLoop s bs (+ i 1) start n acc)))\n\nfn universalNewlines s: String -> String\n  (if (stringContains? s \"\\r\") (let [(bs (stringToBytes s))] (catAll (crLoop s bs 0 0 (bytesLength bs) (list)))) s)\n\nfn lines s: String -> (List String)\n  (splitByte s 10)\n\nfn sectionBody secs: (List Section) shown: (List Int64) -> String\n  (joinWith (map (fn [(p (Pair Section Int64))] -> String\n                     (str \" :\" (pairFirst p).key \" (\" (joinWith (listTake (pairFirst p).items (pairSecond p)) \" \") \")\"))\n                   (zip secs shown)) \"\")\n\nfn sectionMore secs: (List Section) shown: (List Int64) -> String\n  (str \" :more (\" (joinWith (map (fn [(p (Pair Section Int64))] -> String\n                                     (str \":\" (pairFirst p).key \" \" (stringFromInt64 (- (listLength (pairFirst p).items) (pairSecond p)))))\n                                   (zip secs shown)) \" \") \")\")\n\nfn shrinkLast shown: (List Int64) -> (Option (List Int64))\n  (let [(rev (listReverse shown))]\n    (mt (shrinkFirstPositive rev (list))\n      ((some r) (some (listReverse r)))\n      ((none) (none))))\n\nfn shrinkFirstPositive xs: (List Int64) acc: (List Int64) -> (Option (List Int64))\n  (mt (listHead xs)\n    ((none) (none))\n    ((some x) (if (> x 0)\n                (some (listAppend (listReverse acc) (cons (- x 1) (optionOr (listTail xs) (list)))))\n                (shrinkFirstPositive (optionOr (listTail xs) (list)) (cons x acc)))))\n\nfn fitLoop head: String secs: (List Section) tail: String what: String shown: (List Int64) -> (Result String String)\n  (let [(receipt (str head (sectionBody secs shown) (sectionMore secs shown) tail \")\"))]\n    (if (< (byteLen receipt) (receiptMax))\n      (ok receipt)\n      (mt (shrinkLast shown)\n        ((some next) (fitLoop head secs tail what next))\n        ((none) (err (rejectLine \"ERR_RECEIPT_TOO_LARGE\" (str what \" receipt exceeds \" (stringFromInt64 (receiptMax)) \" bytes with every list empty\") \"\"))))))\n\nfn fitReceipt head: String secs: (List Section) tail: String what: String -> (Result String String)\n  (fitLoop head secs tail what (map (fn [(s Section)] -> Int64 (min s.limit (listLength s.items))) secs))\n\nfn closeMatches word: String names: (List String) n: Int64 cutoff: Float64 -> (List String)\n  (sim/getCloseMatches word names n cutoff)\n")
(:file :tree "tc1" :path "asl/tools/observe/memory.asl" :text "(module ws/asl/tools/observe/memory\n  :x [topLevelForms observeMemory!]\n  :i [(ws/asl/tools/observe/common :a c)])\n\nfn ledgerCap -> Int64\n  40\n\nfn formsLoop bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 depth: Int64 forms: Int64 inStr: Bool inComment: Bool -> Int64\n  (if (>= i n)\n    forms\n    (let [(b (bytesGet bs i))]\n      (cond\n        (inComment (formsLoop bs (+ i 1) n depth forms inStr (!= b 10)))\n        (inStr (cond ((= b 92) (formsLoop bs (+ i 2) n depth forms true false))\n                     ((= b 34) (formsLoop bs (+ i 1) n depth forms false false))\n                     (else (formsLoop bs (+ i 1) n depth forms true false))))\n        ((= b 34) (formsLoop bs (+ i 1) n depth forms true false))\n        ((= b 59) (formsLoop bs (+ i 1) n depth forms false true))\n        ((or (= b 40) (= b 91) (= b 123)) (formsLoop bs (+ i 1) n (+ depth 1) (if (= depth 0) (+ forms 1) forms) false false))\n        ((or (= b 41) (= b 93) (= b 125)) (formsLoop bs (+ i 1) n (max 0 (- depth 1)) forms false false))\n        (else (formsLoop bs (+ i 1) n depth forms false false)))))\n\nfn topLevelForms data: String -> Int64\n  (let [(bs (stringToBytes data))] (formsLoop bs 0 (bytesLength bs) 0 0 false false))\n\nfn ledgerStats! path: String -> (Result (Pair Int64 Int64) String)\n  (mt (fileReadString path)\n    ((ok data) (ok (pair (topLevelForms data) (stringLength data))))\n    ((err e) (err e)))\n\nfn listDir! path: String -> (Result (List String) String)\n  (dirList path)\n\nfn walkSum! dir: String -> (Result (Pair Int64 Int64) String)\n  (mt (listDir! dir)\n    ((err e) (err e))\n    ((ok names)\n      (fold (fn [(acc (Result (Pair Int64 Int64) String)) (name String)] -> (Result (Pair Int64 Int64) String)\n              (mt acc\n                ((err e) (err e))\n                ((ok tot)\n                  (let [(full (c/joinPath dir name))]\n                    (cond\n                      ((c/isDir? full)\n                        (if (c/isLink? full)\n                          (ok tot)\n                          (mt (walkSum! full) ((ok s) (ok (pair (+ (pairFirst tot) (pairFirst s)) (+ (pairSecond tot) (pairSecond s))))) ((err e) (err e)))))\n                      ((stringEndsWith? name \".asn\")\n                        (mt (ledgerStats! full) ((ok s) (ok (pair (+ (pairFirst tot) (pairFirst s)) (+ (pairSecond tot) (pairSecond s))))) ((err e) (err e))))\n                      (else (ok tot)))))))\n            (ok (pair 0 0)) names)))\n\n(schema Ledger (:f path String) (:f forms Int64) (:f bytes Int64))\n\nfn ledgerForm l: Ledger -> String\n  (str \"(:path \" (c/quoted l.path) \" :forms \" (stringFromInt64 l.forms) \" :bytes \" (stringFromInt64 l.bytes) \")\")\n\nfn entries! mem: String names: (List String) acc: (List Ledger) -> (Result (List Ledger) String)\n  (mt (listHead names)\n    ((none) (ok (listReverse acc)))\n    ((some name)\n      (let [(full (c/joinPath mem name)) (rel (str \".asl/mem/\" name)) (rest (optionOr (listTail names) (list)))]\n        (cond\n          ((and (c/isFile? full) (stringEndsWith? name \".asn\"))\n            (mt (ledgerStats! full) ((ok s) (entries! mem rest (cons (Ledger :path rel :forms (pairFirst s) :bytes (pairSecond s)) acc))) ((err e) (err e))))\n          ((c/isDir? full)\n            (mt (walkSum! full) ((ok s) (entries! mem rest (cons (Ledger :path (str rel \"/\") :forms (pairFirst s) :bytes (pairSecond s)) acc))) ((err e) (err e))))\n          (else (entries! mem rest acc))))))\n\nfn ! observeMemory! root: String ctx: c/Ctx -> (Result String String)\n  (let [(mem (c/joinPath root \".asl/mem\"))]\n    (if (not (c/isDir? mem))\n      (err (c/rejectLine \"ERR_PATH_NOT_FOUND\" (str \"no .asl/mem directory under \" root) \"\"))\n      (mt (listDir! mem)\n        ((err e) (err (c/rejectLine \"ERR_IO\" e \"\")))\n        ((ok names)\n          (mt (entries! mem names (list))\n            ((err e) (err (c/rejectLine \"ERR_IO\" e \"\")))\n            ((ok ls)\n              (mt (c/shortRev! root ctx)\n                ((err e) (err e))\n                ((ok rev)\n                  (let [(shown (listTake ls (ledgerCap)))]\n                    (ok (str \"(:observe :dim memory :rev \" rev \" :ledgers (\" (c/joinWith (map ledgerForm shown) \" \") \") :more \"\n                             (stringFromInt64 (- (listLength ls) (listLength shown))) \")\")))))))))))\n")
(:file :tree "tc1" :path "asl/tools/observe/session.asl" :text "(module ws/asl/tools/observe/session\n  :x [JVal jsonParse pyStr truthy? fnmatch? ownsCover? ownsMeet readJournal observeSession!]\n  :i [(ws/asl/tools/observe/common :a c)])\n\nfn staleAfter -> Int64\n  1800\n\nfn pathsCap -> Int64\n  8\n\nfn alnum? k: Int64 -> Bool\n  (or (and (>= k 48) (<= k 57)) (and (>= k 65) (<= k 90)) (and (>= k 97) (<= k 122)))\n\nfn alpha? k: Int64 -> Bool\n  (or (and (>= k 65) (<= k 90)) (and (>= k 97) (<= k 122)))\n\nfn sessionId? s: String -> Bool\n  (let [(bs (stringToBytes s)) (n (bytesLength bs))]\n    (and (> n 0) (alnum? (bytesGet bs 0))\n         (listAll? (fn [(i Int64)] -> Bool (let [(k (bytesGet bs i))] (or (alnum? k) (= k 46) (= k 95) (= k 45)))) (range 1 n))))\n\n(enum JVal\n  (:c jNull [])\n  (:c jBool [(b Bool)])\n  (:c jInt [(digits String)])\n  (:c jFloat [(x Float64)])\n  (:c jStr [(s String)])\n  (:c jArr [(xs (List JVal))])\n  (:c jObj [(kvs (List (Pair String JVal)))]))\n\n(schema JP (:f v JVal) (:f at Int64))\n\nfn byteAt bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 -> Int64\n  (if (< i n) (bytesGet bs i) -1)\n\nfn skipWs bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 -> Int64\n  (let [(b (byteAt bs i n))]\n    (if (or (= b 32) (= b 9) (= b 10) (= b 13)) (skipWs bs (+ i 1) n) i))\n\nfn sliceOf s: String a: Int64 b: Int64 -> String\n  (optionOr (stringSlice s a b) \"\")\n\nfn digitsEnd bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 -> Int64\n  (let [(b (byteAt bs i n))] (if (and (>= b 48) (<= b 57)) (digitsEnd bs (+ i 1) n) i))\n\nfn hexVal b: Int64 -> Int64\n  (cond ((and (>= b 48) (<= b 57)) (- b 48)) ((and (>= b 97) (<= b 102)) (- b 87)) ((and (>= b 65) (<= b 70)) (- b 55)) (else -1))\n\nfn hex4 bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 -> Int64\n  (if (> (+ i 4) n)\n    -1\n    (let [(a (hexVal (bytesGet bs i))) (b (hexVal (bytesGet bs (+ i 1)))) (d (hexVal (bytesGet bs (+ i 2)))) (e (hexVal (bytesGet bs (+ i 3))))]\n      (if (or (< a 0) (< b 0) (< d 0) (< e 0)) -1 (+ (* a 4096) (* b 256) (* d 16) e))))\n\nfn byteStr k: Int64 -> String\n  (optionOr (stringSlice (byteTable) k (+ k 1)) \"\")\n\nfn byteTable -> String\n  \"\\x00\\x01\\x02\\x03\\x04\\x05\\x06\\x07\\x08\\x09\\x0a\\x0b\\x0c\\x0d\\x0e\\x0f\\x10\\x11\\x12\\x13\\x14\\x15\\x16\\x17\\x18\\x19\\x1a\\x1b\\x1c\\x1d\\x1e\\x1f\\x20\\x21\\x22\\x23\\x24\\x25\\x26\\x27\\x28\\x29\\x2a\\x2b\\x2c\\x2d\\x2e\\x2f\\x30\\x31\\x32\\x33\\x34\\x35\\x36\\x37\\x38\\x39\\x3a\\x3b\\x3c\\x3d\\x3e\\x3f\\x40\\x41\\x42\\x43\\x44\\x45\\x46\\x47\\x48\\x49\\x4a\\x4b\\x4c\\x4d\\x4e\\x4f\\x50\\x51\\x52\\x53\\x54\\x55\\x56\\x57\\x58\\x59\\x5a\\x5b\\x5c\\x5d\\x5e\\x5f\\x60\\x61\\x62\\x63\\x64\\x65\\x66\\x67\\x68\\x69\\x6a\\x6b\\x6c\\x6d\\x6e\\x6f\\x70\\x71\\x72\\x73\\x74\\x75\\x76\\x77\\x78\\x79\\x7a\\x7b\\x7c\\x7d\\x7e\\x7f\\x80\\x81\\x82\\x83\\x84\\x85\\x86\\x87\\x88\\x89\\x8a\\x8b\\x8c\\x8d\\x8e\\x8f\\x90\\x91\\x92\\x93\\x94\\x95\\x96\\x97\\x98\\x99\\x9a\\x9b\\x9c\\x9d\\x9e\\x9f\\xa0\\xa1\\xa2\\xa3\\xa4\\xa5\\xa6\\xa7\\xa8\\xa9\\xaa\\xab\\xac\\xad\\xae\\xaf\\xb0\\xb1\\xb2\\xb3\\xb4\\xb5\\xb6\\xb7\\xb8\\xb9\\xba\\xbb\\xbc\\xbd\\xbe\\xbf\\xc0\\xc1\\xc2\\xc3\\xc4\\xc5\\xc6\\xc7\\xc8\\xc9\\xca\\xcb\\xcc\\xcd\\xce\\xcf\\xd0\\xd1\\xd2\\xd3\\xd4\\xd5\\xd6\\xd7\\xd8\\xd9\\xda\\xdb\\xdc\\xdd\\xde\\xdf\\xe0\\xe1\\xe2\\xe3\\xe4\\xe5\\xe6\\xe7\\xe8\\xe9\\xea\\xeb\\xec\\xed\\xee\\xef\\xf0\\xf1\\xf2\\xf3\\xf4\\xf5\\xf6\\xf7\\xf8\\xf9\\xfa\\xfb\\xfc\\xfd\\xfe\\xff\"\n\nfn utf8Of cp: Int64 -> String\n  (cond\n    ((< cp 128) (byteStr cp))\n    ((< cp 2048) (str (byteStr (+ 192 (/ cp 64))) (byteStr (+ 128 (mod cp 64)))))\n    ((< cp 65536) (str (byteStr (+ 224 (/ cp 4096))) (byteStr (+ 128 (mod (/ cp 64) 64))) (byteStr (+ 128 (mod cp 64)))))\n    (else (str (byteStr (+ 240 (/ cp 262144))) (byteStr (+ 128 (mod (/ cp 4096) 64))) (byteStr (+ 128 (mod (/ cp 64) 64))) (byteStr (+ 128 (mod cp 64))))))\n\nfn strBody s: String bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 start: Int64 acc: (List String) -> (Result JP String)\n  (let [(b (byteAt bs i n))]\n    (cond\n      ((< b 0) (err \"Unterminated string\"))\n      ((= b 34) (ok (JP :v (jStr (c/catAll (listReverse (cons (sliceOf s start i) acc)))) :at (+ i 1))))\n      ((< b 32) (err \"Invalid control character\"))\n      ((= b 92)\n        (let [(e (byteAt bs (+ i 1) n)) (pre (cons (sliceOf s start i) acc))]\n          (cond\n            ((= e 34) (strBody s bs (+ i 2) n (+ i 2) (cons \"\\\"\" pre)))\n            ((= e 92) (strBody s bs (+ i 2) n (+ i 2) (cons \"\\\\\" pre)))\n            ((= e 47) (strBody s bs (+ i 2) n (+ i 2) (cons \"/\" pre)))\n            ((= e 98) (strBody s bs (+ i 2) n (+ i 2) (cons \"\\x08\" pre)))\n            ((= e 102) (strBody s bs (+ i 2) n (+ i 2) (cons \"\\x0c\" pre)))\n            ((= e 110) (strBody s bs (+ i 2) n (+ i 2) (cons \"\\n\" pre)))\n            ((= e 114) (strBody s bs (+ i 2) n (+ i 2) (cons \"\\r\" pre)))\n            ((= e 116) (strBody s bs (+ i 2) n (+ i 2) (cons \"\\t\" pre)))\n            ((= e 117)\n              (let [(u (hex4 bs (+ i 2) n))]\n                (cond\n                  ((< u 0) (err \"Invalid \\\\uXXXX escape\"))\n                  ((and (>= u 55296) (<= u 56319) (= (byteAt bs (+ i 6) n) 92) (= (byteAt bs (+ i 7) n) 117))\n                    (let [(lo (hex4 bs (+ i 8) n))]\n                      (if (and (>= lo 56320) (<= lo 57343))\n                        (strBody s bs (+ i 12) n (+ i 12) (cons (utf8Of (+ 65536 (* (- u 55296) 1024) (- lo 56320))) pre))\n                        (strBody s bs (+ i 6) n (+ i 6) (cons (utf8Of u) pre)))))\n                  (else (strBody s bs (+ i 6) n (+ i 6) (cons (utf8Of u) pre))))))\n            (else (err \"Invalid \\\\escape\")))))\n      (else (strBody s bs (+ i 1) n start acc))))\n\nfn numberAt s: String bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 -> (Result JP String)\n  (let [(neg (= (byteAt bs i n) 45))\n        (j (if neg (+ i 1) i))\n        (b (byteAt bs j n))]\n    (cond\n      ((and neg (= b 73) (= (sliceOf s j (+ j 8)) \"Infinity\")) (ok (JP :v (jFloat (floatNegInf)) :at (+ j 8))))\n      ((not (and (>= b 48) (<= b 57))) (err \"Expecting value\"))\n      (else\n        (let [(intEnd (if (= b 48) (+ j 1) (digitsEnd bs j n)))\n              (fracEnd (if (and (= (byteAt bs intEnd n) 46) (let [(d (byteAt bs (+ intEnd 1) n))] (and (>= d 48) (<= d 57)))) (digitsEnd bs (+ intEnd 1) n) intEnd))\n              (e (byteAt bs fracEnd n))\n              (expStart (if (or (= e 101) (= e 69)) (let [(sg (byteAt bs (+ fracEnd 1) n))] (if (or (= sg 43) (= sg 45)) (+ fracEnd 2) (+ fracEnd 1))) -1))\n              (expEnd (if (and (>= expStart 0) (let [(d (byteAt bs expStart n))] (and (>= d 48) (<= d 57)))) (digitsEnd bs expStart n) fracEnd))\n              (text (sliceOf s i expEnd))]\n          (if (and (= fracEnd intEnd) (= expEnd fracEnd))\n            (let [(mag (c/lstripChars (sliceOf s j intEnd) \"0\"))]\n              (ok (JP :v (jInt (if (stringEmpty? mag) \"0\" (if neg (str \"-\" mag) mag))) :at expEnd)))\n            (mt (stringToFloat64 text)\n              ((some f) (ok (JP :v (jFloat f) :at expEnd)))\n              ((none) (err \"Invalid number\"))))))))\n\nfn valueAt s: String bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 depth: Int64 -> (Result JP String)\n  (let [(b (byteAt bs i n))]\n    (cond\n      ((> depth 900) (err \"RecursionError\"))\n      ((= b 34) (strBody s bs (+ i 1) n (+ i 1) (list)))\n      ((= b 123) (objectAt s bs (skipWs bs (+ i 1) n) n depth (list) true))\n      ((= b 91) (arrayAt s bs (skipWs bs (+ i 1) n) n depth (list) true))\n      ((= (sliceOf s i (+ i 4)) \"null\") (ok (JP :v (jNull) :at (+ i 4))))\n      ((= (sliceOf s i (+ i 4)) \"true\") (ok (JP :v (jBool true) :at (+ i 4))))\n      ((= (sliceOf s i (+ i 5)) \"false\") (ok (JP :v (jBool false) :at (+ i 5))))\n      ((= (sliceOf s i (+ i 3)) \"NaN\") (ok (JP :v (jFloat (floatNan)) :at (+ i 3))))\n      ((= (sliceOf s i (+ i 8)) \"Infinity\") (ok (JP :v (jFloat (floatInf)) :at (+ i 8))))\n      (else (numberAt s bs i n))))\n\nfn arrayAt s: String bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 depth: Int64 acc: (List JVal) first: Bool -> (Result JP String)\n  (if (and first (= (byteAt bs i n) 93))\n    (ok (JP :v (jArr (list)) :at (+ i 1)))\n    (mt (valueAt s bs i n (+ depth 1))\n      ((err e) (err e))\n      ((ok p)\n        (let [(j (skipWs bs p.at n)) (b (byteAt bs j n)) (acc2 (cons p.v acc))]\n          (cond\n            ((= b 93) (ok (JP :v (jArr (listReverse acc2)) :at (+ j 1))))\n            ((= b 44) (arrayAt s bs (skipWs bs (+ j 1) n) n depth acc2 false))\n            (else (err \"Expecting ',' delimiter\")))))))\n\nfn putKey kvs: (List (Pair String JVal)) k: String v: JVal -> (List (Pair String JVal))\n  (if (listAny? (fn [(p (Pair String JVal))] -> Bool (= (pairFirst p) k)) kvs)\n    (map (fn [(p (Pair String JVal))] -> (Pair String JVal) (if (= (pairFirst p) k) (pair k v) p)) kvs)\n    (listAppend kvs (list (pair k v))))\n\nfn objectAt s: String bs: Bytes i: Int64 n: Int64 depth: Int64 acc: (List (Pair String JVal)) first: Bool -> (Result JP String)\n  (let [(b (byteAt bs i n))]\n    (cond\n      ((and first (= b 125)) (ok (JP :v (jObj (list)) :at (+ i 1))))\n      ((!= b 34) (err \"Expecting property name enclosed in double quotes\"))\n      (else\n        (mt (strBody s bs (+ i 1) n (+ i 1) (list))\n          ((err e) (err e))\n          ((ok kp)\n            (let [(j (skipWs bs kp.at n))]\n              (if (!= (byteAt bs j n) 58)\n                (err \"Expecting ':' delimiter\")\n                (mt (valueAt s bs (skipWs bs (+ j 1) n) n (+ depth 1))\n                  ((err e) (err e))\n                  ((ok vp)\n                    (let [(key (mt kp.v ((jStr k) k) (_ \"\")))\n                          (acc2 (putKey acc key vp.v))\n                          (m (skipWs bs vp.at n))\n                          (d (byteAt bs m n))]\n                      (cond\n                        ((= d 125) (ok (JP :v (jObj acc2) :at (+ m 1))))\n                        ((= d 44) (objectAt s bs (skipWs bs (+ m 1) n) n depth acc2 false))\n                        (else (err \"Expect